<edge source="232736e7-acf8-4d22-b841-096230540a60" target="e1df3d86-8de9-47d8-afa0-06dda8b550f2">
  <data key="d3">As the primary beneficiary, Matthew Scott Thompson is entitled to receive the full death benefit if Jessica Lynn Thompson passes away. This role complements her position as the policy owner, though does not depend on it directly.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="232736e7-acf8-4d22-b841-096230540a60" target="b2a30ea9-f6f0-4538-a482-ad994edbeb6b">
  <data key="d3">As the primary beneficiary entitled to 100% of the death benefit, Matthew Scott Thompson has a direct claim on the proceeds due to his marital relationship with Jessica Lynn Thompson, who is the insured individual.</data>
  <data key="d4">spouse of insured</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="232736e7-acf8-4d22-b841-096230540a60" target="50af0d4a-2680-43a9-9d6f-6eec2018a92a">
  <data key="d3">Matthew Scott Thompson being designated as the sole primary beneficiary reflects the intended distribution of the death benefit upon Jessica’s passing. His status as the exclusive recipient is consistent with the policy’s stated beneficiary structure, independent of but contextualized by Jessica’s personal information such as her DOB.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="232736e7-acf8-4d22-b841-096230540a60" target="db5f42b7-e216-4454-b4f0-97dfc9c2dbc6">
  <data key="d3">As the sole primary beneficiary entitled to 100% of the death benefit, Matthew Scott Thompson will receive the $500,000 payout under Option 1 (Level), which guarantees a consistent sum regardless of timing.</data>
  <data key="d4">receives from</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="232736e7-acf8-4d22-b841-096230540a60" target="5208ec0c-2803-47eb-b876-385a82abb6a6">
  <data key="d3">Matthew Scott Thompson being the sole primary beneficiary implies he receives the entire death benefit upon Jessica’s passing.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="232736e7-acf8-4d22-b841-096230540a60" target="59864efa-99a1-4d3b-bba3-8572dfaf53ee">
  <data key="d3">Matthew’s exclusive claim to the primary beneficiary position aligns with his identity as Jessica’s legally recognized spouse, reinforcing the legitimacy of the arrangement.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="232736e7-acf8-4d22-b841-096230540a60" target="3bf01cd5-6749-4600-bf13-16b3896d7e14">
  <data key="d3">Matthew Scott Thompson being the full primary beneficiary establishes his right to receive proceeds if he outlives Jessica. This role is separate from the contingent beneficiary, who receives funds only if no primary beneficiaries survive.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="232736e7-acf8-4d22-b841-096230540a60" target="3fd07a47-8608-4719-b77f-03989041a449">
  <data key="d3">Matthew Scott Thompson is designated as the sole recipient of the death benefit if he survives Jessica Lynn Thompson. This establishes his priority claim, setting up the condition under which the contingent beneficiary would activate.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
