<edge source="3bf01cd5-6749-4600-bf13-16b3896d7e14" target="38b91269-d890-44e6-8d3e-f8bfc905c69a">
  <data key="d3">Designating the Thompson Family Trust as the contingent beneficiary ensures succession planning aligns with estate goals. This choice is consistent with policies like Equity-Indexed Universal Life, which offer flexible structures suitable for complex beneficiaries.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3bf01cd5-6749-4600-bf13-16b3896d7e14" target="e1df3d86-8de9-47d8-afa0-06dda8b550f2">
  <data key="d3">The Thompson Family Trust serves as the contingent beneficiary, meaning its eligibility depends on the policy being owned by someone—here, Jessica Lynn Thompson—who has the right to assign such designations.</data>
  <data key="d4">required by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3bf01cd5-6749-4600-bf13-16b3896d7e14" target="5208ec0c-2803-47eb-b876-385a82abb6a6">
  <data key="d3">If the Thompson Family Trust is named as the contingent beneficiary, it means it serves as a backup recipient when the primary beneficiary, Matthew Scott Thompson, cannot inherit due to prior death or disqualification.</data>
  <data key="d4">primary for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3bf01cd5-6749-4600-bf13-16b3896d7e14" target="3fd07a47-8608-4719-b77f-03989041a449">
  <data key="d3">The Thompson Family Trust is named as the contingent beneficiary, and it exclusively holds the entire contingent share of the death benefit, ensuring complete control over that portion.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3bf01cd5-6749-4600-bf13-16b3896d7e14" target="232736e7-acf8-4d22-b841-096230540a60">
  <data key="d3">The existence of the Thompson Family Trust as the contingent beneficiary ensures that benefits are directed appropriately if the primary beneficiary predeceases Jessica or fails to claim. This designation complements the primary beneficiary’s status without altering it.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
