<edge source="3fd07a47-8608-4719-b77f-03989041a449" target="e1df3d86-8de9-47d8-afa0-06dda8b550f2">
  <data key="d3">The Thompson Family Trust serves as the contingent beneficiary, meaning it receives the death benefit only after the primary beneficiary—Matthew Scott Thompson—if applicable; this arrangement reflects decisions made by the policy owner, Jessica Lynn Thompson.</data>
  <data key="d4">contingent role</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3fd07a47-8608-4719-b77f-03989041a449" target="b2a30ea9-f6f0-4538-a482-ad994edbeb6b">
  <data key="d3">The Thompson Family Trust is appointed as the complete contingent beneficiary, reflecting its legal standing in receiving proceeds only after the primary beneficiary’s claim fails, based on the insured being Jessica Lynn Thompson.</data>
  <data key="d4">assigned to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3fd07a47-8608-4719-b77f-03989041a449" target="3bf01cd5-6749-4600-bf13-16b3896d7e14">
  <data key="d3">As the entity holding 100% of the contingent beneficiary share, the Thompson Family Trust is formally designated as the sole contingent beneficiary of the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">defined by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3fd07a47-8608-4719-b77f-03989041a449" target="59864efa-99a1-4d3b-bba3-8572dfaf53ee">
  <data key="d3">The Thompson Family Trust being the sole contingent beneficiary ensures succession planning continuity should Matthew Scott Thompson, the primary beneficiary, be unable to claim the proceeds, reinforcing the estate plan established through the marriage.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3fd07a47-8608-4719-b77f-03989041a449" target="232736e7-acf8-4d22-b841-096230540a60">
  <data key="d3">If Matthew Scott Thompson does not survive Jessica Lynn Thompson or declines the benefit, the Thompson Family Trust becomes entitled to the entire death benefit, serving as the backup recipient in the succession plan.</data>
  <data key="d4">follows</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
