<edge source="eec22563-c8f9-4930-abc2-6252103b7b77" target="1c5eba0f-2f29-43d1-b13a-bc342d4f4ae4">
  <data key="d3">The Floor Rate serves as a protective measure within Index Accounts, ensuring that even if the underlying index performs poorly, the account still earns at least zero percent interest, thereby reinforcing the core function of these accounts.</data>
  <data key="d4">enhances</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eec22563-c8f9-4930-abc2-6252103b7b77" target="1d4b712e-5e26-4cf9-a7ad-301c683e58e3">
  <data key="d3">The floor rate protects policyholders from losing money when markets decline; however, its effectiveness depends on whether the cap rate allows meaningful upside despite limits on growth.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eec22563-c8f9-4930-abc2-6252103b7b77" target="a3259e6d-b7fd-4e82-92f7-523ed8d8a955">
  <data key="d3">The Floor Rate sets the lowest possible interest rate (0%), safeguarding policyholders from losses during downturns. This safety net complements the Participation Rate, which dictates how much of any market gains are applied to the account.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eec22563-c8f9-4930-abc2-6252103b7b77" target="42ce1796-4b22-4fa1-987f-341d1746d7f3">
  <data key="d3">The Floor Rate ensures that even if the Point-to-Point Method results in a negative return, the credited interest rate cannot fall below 0%, thus safeguarding policyholders from losses.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eec22563-c8f9-4930-abc2-6252103b7b77" target="492399d4-a4a8-470a-b04c-a4e38ca316d2">
  <data key="d3">The Floor Rate ensures no negative returns, providing downside protection; this complements the Cap Rate, which limits upside gains, together forming symmetric risk controls in the indexing method.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eec22563-c8f9-4930-abc2-6252103b7b77" target="e6aa2762-a82e-4371-9d8e-da19a25dd6d1">
  <data key="d3">The Floor Rate ensures no negative crediting on any index account, providing downside protection. This principle applies universally, including to the S&amp;P 500 Index Account described in the second sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">applies to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eec22563-c8f9-4930-abc2-6252103b7b77" target="a4c6faf8-57d8-4d84-affb-d94570b3ae60">
  <data key="d3">The Floor Rate ensures no negative returns; specifically, the S&amp;P 500 Index Account maintains a 0% Floor, aligning with the defined protection mechanism.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eec22563-c8f9-4930-abc2-6252103b7b77" target="a0671d34-e31b-4b17-8ed5-6a9d495c5148">
  <data key="d3">The Floor Rate ensures a minimum credit of 0%, safeguarding policyholders during downturns across any crediting period, such as the one-year cycle defined for the S&amp;P 500 Index Account.</data>
  <data key="d4">applies to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eec22563-c8f9-4930-abc2-6252103b7b77" target="62714aed-4640-40fa-9927-1e7eaaddb24c">
  <data key="d3">The Floor Rate ensures no negative crediting on any index account, providing downside protection regardless of market movement. This safeguards the NASDAQ-100 Index Account, among others, from losing value during downturns.</data>
  <data key="d4">applies to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eec22563-c8f9-4930-abc2-6252103b7b77" target="bce094ed-5c85-40d1-800b-e0894835715b">
  <data key="d3">The Floor Rate ensures no negative returns; the NASDAQ-100 account explicitly uses a 0% floor, illustrating how the protection works in practice.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eec22563-c8f9-4930-abc2-6252103b7b77" target="4144da65-9775-496c-b601-6cbcd31e5849">
  <data key="d3">The Floor Rate ensures no negative returns, providing stability; this complements the Cap Rate, such as the 9.0% limit on the NASDAQ-100, which controls maximum gains.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
