  <data key="d3">The Floor Rate ensures a minimum 0% credit regardless of market movement, providing downside protection during the crediting period defined for each index account.</data>
  <data key="d4">protects during</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eec22563-c8f9-4930-abc2-6252103b7b77" target="a5cf74c6-3010-4b87-83b5-452662af8369">
  <data key="d3">The definition of Floor Rate as a safeguard against negative returns is illustrated by the Global Diversified Index Account's explicit 0% floor, demonstrating how the abstract concept applies concretely.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eec22563-c8f9-4930-abc2-6252103b7b77" target="13cdba53-929e-487b-9dac-c7e31bdd92a0">
  <data key="d3">The Floor Rate ensures no negative returns regardless of market movement, providing stability. This contrasts with the Cap Rate, such as the 8.5% limit on the Global Diversified Index, which restricts maximum gains.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eec22563-c8f9-4930-abc2-6252103b7b77" target="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes the Floor Rate as a safeguard guaranteeing zero interest during market declines; fact_sentence_2 demonstrates its practical effect when the index falls by 5%, confirming it prevents any loss.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eec22563-c8f9-4930-abc2-6252103b7b77" target="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7">
  <data key="d3">The Floor Rate ensures zero interest credit during market declines, which explains why a 5% drop results in 0% credited interest.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eec22563-c8f9-4930-abc2-6252103b7b77" target="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 explains that the Floor Rate ensures no negative returns, and fact_sentence_2 confirms this protective mechanism is implemented at 0%, supporting the idea that market declines do not affect the account value.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eec22563-c8f9-4930-abc2-6252103b7b77" target="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1">
  <data key="d3">The Floor Rate of 0% guarantees that the policyholder will never earn less than 0% interest, meaning the worst-case scenario—earning nothing—is precisely what the floor protects against.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eec22563-c8f9-4930-abc2-6252103b7b77" target="70667dae-ff8c-4bac-bf04-03807ddb6bd7">
  <data key="d3">The Floor Rate of 0% ensures that market declines do not reduce the account value, directly enabling the guarantee stated in fact_sentence_2 that principal remains intact despite falling markets.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eec22563-c8f9-4930-abc2-6252103b7b77" target="e56d9b1f-113b-4961-abbd-159d8047aeca">
  <data key="d3">The Floor Rate ensures no losses occur even if markets decline, while the 100% participation rate on the Global Diversified Index allows full exposure to positive market movements, together forming a balanced risk-return structure.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eec22563-c8f9-4930-abc2-6252103b7b77" target="326a19f6-3d06-4cde-a9f0-0b1923801873">
  <data key="d3">The Floor Rate ensures no negative returns, while the 8.5% cap limits upside gain potential specifically for the Global Diversified Index Account, illustrating balanced risk control features.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="eec22563-c8f9-4930-abc2-6252103b7b77" target="665dbf69-ad45-49be-8a49-a811282557e1">
  <data key="d3">The Floor Rate ensures no losses when index values decline, which depends on the correct calculation of index percentage changes outlined in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
