<edge source="a3259e6d-b7fd-4e82-92f7-523ed8d8a955" target="1c5eba0f-2f29-43d1-b13a-bc342d4f4ae4">
  <data key="d3">The Participation Rate determines how much of the index's gain is reflected in the account’s interest credit, making it a critical component of how an Index Account functions.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a3259e6d-b7fd-4e82-92f7-523ed8d8a955" target="1d4b712e-5e26-4cf9-a7ad-301c683e58e3">
  <data key="d3">The Participation Rate dictates how much of the index's gain beyond zero is passed through, but its impact is constrained by the Cap Rate, which acts as a ceiling on total crediting.</data>
  <data key="d4">limited by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a3259e6d-b7fd-4e82-92f7-523ed8d8a955" target="eec22563-c8f9-4930-abc2-6252103b7b77">
  <data key="d3">The Participation Rate defines what portion of index growth gets credited to the account, working alongside the Floor Rate—which guarantees at least zero return—to ensure balanced risk management and reward sharing.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a3259e6d-b7fd-4e82-92f7-523ed8d8a955" target="42ce1796-4b22-4fa1-987f-341d1746d7f3">
  <data key="d3">The Participation Rate determines what portion of the index's growth is credited, but only if calculated via the Point-to-Point Method, which measures year-over-year changes.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a3259e6d-b7fd-4e82-92f7-523ed8d8a955" target="492399d4-a4a8-470a-b04c-a4e38ca316d2">
  <data key="d3">The Participation Rate determines what portion of the index's growth is credited to the account, while the Cap sets the upper limit on that credited amount. Together, they shape the potential return, though neither depends on the other numerically.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a3259e6d-b7fd-4e82-92f7-523ed8d8a955" target="faf66c9e-da0e-4813-9561-2d1480419596">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence defines the Participation Rate as the proportion of index gains credited to an account. This definition is concretely illustrated by the second sentence, which states that the S&amp;P 500 Index Account uses a 100% participation rate.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a3259e6d-b7fd-4e82-92f7-523ed8d8a955" target="a4c6faf8-57d8-4d84-affb-d94570b3ae60">
  <data key="d3">The concept of Participation Rate determines how much of the index's growth is passed on to the policyholder, whereas the Floor ensures losses aren't transferred when the index declines. These elements together shape the overall performance mechanism.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a3259e6d-b7fd-4e82-92f7-523ed8d8a955" target="a0671d34-e31b-4b17-8ed5-6a9d495c5148">
  <data key="d3">The Participation Rate determines how much of the index’s gain is credited during each crediting period, such as the one-year cycle specified for the S&amp;P 500 Index Account.</data>
  <data key="d4">applies during</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a3259e6d-b7fd-4e82-92f7-523ed8d8a955" target="62714aed-4640-40fa-9927-1e7eaaddb24c">
  <data key="d3">The definition of Participation Rate establishes a core concept used across all index accounts, providing context necessary to understand how gains are calculated in accounts like the NASDAQ-100.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a3259e6d-b7fd-4e82-92f7-523ed8d8a955" target="4144da65-9775-496c-b601-6cbcd31e5849">
  <data key="d3">The Participation Rate determines what portion of the NASDAQ-100’s gain is eligible for crediting, but this amount is capped at 9.0%, limiting total potential credits regardless of index performance.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a3259e6d-b7fd-4e82-92f7-523ed8d8a955" target="bce094ed-5c85-40d1-800b-e0894835715b">
  <data key="d3">The Participation Rate determines how much of the index's gain is applied to the account balance, while the Floor ensures losses are not passed on during negative periods. These concepts together shape the risk-return profile of indexed accounts.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a3259e6d-b7fd-4e82-92f7-523ed8d8a955" target="32909f74-b806-4169-8ab1-602ea158ef9f">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence establishes the general meaning of Participation Rate as the proportion of index gains credited to an account. The second sentence provides a specific example by stating that the NASDAQ-100 Index Account uses a 100% participation rate, illustrating how the abstract definition operates in practice.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a3259e6d-b7fd-4e82-92f7-523ed8d8a955" target="b0213eb9-bcd3-41f0-9381-ae8e81ac0f24">
  <data key="d3">The definition of Participation Rate describes how much of the index's gain is credited to the account, which operates over a defined time frame such as the one specified in Fact Sentence 2.</data>
  <data key="d4">applies to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a3259e6d-b7fd-4e82-92f7-523ed8d8a955" target="22fdc352-4139-456b-bd73-2207bfdefc4e">
  <data key="d3">The first sentence defines the term "Participation Rate," while the second sentence provides a specific example of it being set at 100% for the Global Diversified Index Account.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a3259e6d-b7fd-4e82-92f7-523ed8d8a955" target="13cdba53-929e-487b-9dac-c7e31bdd92a0">
  <data key="d3">The Participation Rate determines what portion of the index's growth is applied to the account balance, while the Cap sets the upper limit on that amount. Together, they shape the potential returns under the index-based crediting method.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a3259e6d-b7fd-4e82-92f7-523ed8d8a955" target="326a19f6-3d06-4cde-a9f0-0b1923801873">
  <data key="d3">The definition of Participation Rate explains how much of the index’s gain is applied to the account; knowing the Global Diversified Index has an 8.5% cap clarifies the upper limit on potential credits under this rule.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a3259e6d-b7fd-4e82-92f7-523ed8d8a955" target="e56d9b1f-113b-4961-abbd-159d8047aeca">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 defines the concept of Participation Rate, which is directly illustrated by fact_sentence_2 stating that the Global Diversified Index Account applies a 100% participation rate.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a3259e6d-b7fd-4e82-92f7-523ed8d8a955" target="f64306b3-60d7-48b6-82c2-6580397642e1">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 explains how participation rate determines credit share; fact_sentence_2 confirms the Global Diversified account’s 0% floor, reinforcing its risk protection features mentioned in the same context.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a3259e6d-b7fd-4e82-92f7-523ed8d8a955" target="665dbf69-ad45-49be-8a49-a811282557e1">
  <data key="d3">The Participation Rate determines what portion of the index gain, computed via the point-to-point method described here, gets credited to the account.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a3259e6d-b7fd-4e82-92f7-523ed8d8a955" target="27176921-2e5c-44aa-bcf0-40ddf6e140f2">
  <data key="d3">The definition of Participation Rate directly enables the formula used to calculate credited interest, making it essential for understanding how much of the index gain is reflected in the account balance.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a3259e6d-b7fd-4e82-92f7-523ed8d8a955" target="6ff1f4bc-a2b4-4e15-b514-415d803bd39b">
  <data key="d3">The Participation Rate determines how much of the index's gain is applied to interest credits, operating within the broader framework where those credits are limited by a cap and protected by a floor.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a3259e6d-b7fd-4e82-92f7-523ed8d8a955" target="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e">
  <data key="d3">The Participation Rate determines how gains from the indexed account affect the policy’s growth, influencing the account value upon which surrender charges are calculated. Higher participation rates may reduce the effective cost of surrendering later.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a3259e6d-b7fd-4e82-92f7-523ed8d8a955" target="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a">
  <data key="d3">The Participation Rate determines how much of the index's gain increases the Account Value, which is a core component in computing the Cash Surrender Value described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
