</edge>
<edge source="42ce1796-4b22-4fa1-987f-341d1746d7f3" target="1c5eba0f-2f29-43d1-b13a-bc342d4f4ae4">
  <data key="d3">The Point-to-Point Method details the operational mechanics behind interest crediting in an Index Account, providing concrete implementation of the abstract concept introduced in the prior statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42ce1796-4b22-4fa1-987f-341d1746d7f3" target="1d4b712e-5e26-4cf9-a7ad-301c683e58e3">
  <data key="d3">The Point-to-Point Method determines how much interest is earned annually, but its outcome is constrained by the Cap Rate, which prevents exceeding a specified percentage regardless of index growth.</data>
  <data key="d4">constrained by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42ce1796-4b22-4fa1-987f-341d1746d7f3" target="eec22563-c8f9-4930-abc2-6252103b7b77">
  <data key="d3">The Point-to-Point Method determines annual interest credit based on index movement over time, but its effective range is bounded by the Floor Rate, preventing any negative crediting.</data>
  <data key="d4">constrained by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42ce1796-4b22-4fa1-987f-341d1746d7f3" target="a3259e6d-b7fd-4e82-92f7-523ed8d8a955">
  <data key="d3">The Point-to-Point Method establishes how index returns are measured; its results directly determine how much of the gain is subject to the Participation Rate.</data>
  <data key="d4">applies to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42ce1796-4b22-4fa1-987f-341d1746d7f3" target="e6aa2762-a82e-4371-9d8e-da19a25dd6d1">
  <data key="d3">The Point-to-Point Method, defined as annual interest crediting based on index movement, directly applies to the S&amp;P 500 Index Account described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42ce1796-4b22-4fa1-987f-341d1746d7f3" target="492399d4-a4a8-470a-b04c-a4e38ca316d2">
  <data key="d3">The Point-to-Point Method determines annual interest credits based on index performance over a full year; the 10.5% cap limits potential gains for the S&amp;P 500 account under this approach.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42ce1796-4b22-4fa1-987f-341d1746d7f3" target="faf66c9e-da0e-4813-9561-2d1480419596">
  <data key="d3">The Point-to-Point Method establishes the annual basis for calculating interest credits, enabling the application of a 100% Participation Rate specifically for the S&amp;P 500 Index Account.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42ce1796-4b22-4fa1-987f-341d1746d7f3" target="a0671d34-e31b-4b17-8ed5-6a9d495c5148">
  <data key="d3">The Point-to-Point Method involves calculating interest annually based on index movement; this definition explains why the S&amp;P 500 Index Account has a 1-year crediting period.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="42ce1796-4b22-4fa1-987f-341d1746d7f3" target="a4c6faf8-57d8-4d84-affb-d94570b3ae60">
  <data key="d3">The Point-to-Point Method calculates annual interest based on index performance; the 0% floor ensures no negative returns result from this calculation, protecting policyholders against market downturns.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
