  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states the cap rate for the S&amp;P 500 Index Account at 10.5%, while fact sentence 2 specifies that the Global Diversified Index Account has a lower cap of 8.5%. These figures illustrate how different indexes have distinct upper limits on potential gains despite sharing similar structural rules.</data>
