<edge source="faf66c9e-da0e-4813-9561-2d1480419596" target="a3259e6d-b7fd-4e82-92f7-523ed8d8a955">
  <data key="d3">The second sentence gives a specific instance of the Participation Rate being applied—the S&amp;P 500 Index Account has a 100% participation rate. This example clarifies and operationalizes the abstract definition provided in the first sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">applies to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="faf66c9e-da0e-4813-9561-2d1480419596" target="42ce1796-4b22-4fa1-987f-341d1746d7f3">
  <data key="d3">A 100% Participation Rate in the S&amp;P 500 Index Account means full exposure to the index’s gain during the annual Point-to-Point crediting period.</data>
  <data key="d4">applies to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="faf66c9e-da0e-4813-9561-2d1480419596" target="e6aa2762-a82e-4371-9d8e-da19a25dd6d1">
  <data key="d3">The 100% participation rate applies specifically to the S&amp;P 500 Index Account, which was introduced earlier as one of the available index accounts using the annual point-to-point method.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="faf66c9e-da0e-4813-9561-2d1480419596" target="492399d4-a4a8-470a-b04c-a4e38ca316d2">
  <data key="d3">A 100% Participation Rate means the S&amp;P 500 Index Account fully captures any positive movement in the index, subject to the 10.5% Cap Rate limiting total creditable gains.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.9</data>
</edge>
<edge source="faf66c9e-da0e-4813-9561-2d1480419596" target="a4c6faf8-57d8-4d84-affb-d94570b3ae60">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 establishes that the S&amp;P 500 Index Account offers full participation in gains. This complements fact sentence 2, which ensures losses cannot exceed zero, providing downside protection regardless of market movement.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
