  <data key="d3">The NASDAQ-100 Index Account's 0% floor demonstrates the practical application of the general Floor Rate principle described earlier.</data>
  <data key="d4">applies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="bce094ed-5c85-40d1-800b-e0894835715b" target="a3259e6d-b7fd-4e82-92f7-523ed8d8a955">
  <data key="d3">A 0% floor means no negative returns are deducted from the account, regardless of index decline. This complements the Participation Rate, which governs positive return crediting but does not affect downside protection.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
