  <data key="d3">The one-year crediting period governs how returns are calculated annually for the NASDAQ-100 account, influencing overall growth potential, while the Year 4 surrender charge reflects a cost associated with withdrawing funds before maturity. These elements together inform long-term strategy decisions regarding holding duration versus liquidity needs.</data>
