  <data key="d3">The 1-year crediting period defines the timeframe over which the 0% floor applies, ensuring periodic performance evaluation and safeguard against losses across full years.</data>
  <data key="d4">protects over</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7898028b-343b-4195-9f4c-a6280a62d640" target="2b2e3f84-59bf-4a6e-b26c-8b5ae353f6de">
  <data key="d3">The 1-year crediting period for the Global Diversified Index Account establishes a timeframe within which performance is calculated; policyholders can adjust their allocations on each policy anniversary, ensuring alignment with the end of each crediting cycle.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7898028b-343b-4195-9f4c-a6280a62d640" target="65f18412-1464-4177-ad9f-477c8d9091d3">
  <data key="d3">The length of the crediting period for the Global Diversified Index Account determines how often performance is measured, influencing when investors might consider rebalancing. This timing could indirectly affect decisions around exceeding the free reallocation threshold, leading to fees.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7898028b-343b-4195-9f4c-a6280a62d640" target="665dbf69-ad45-49be-8a49-a811282557e1">
  <data key="d3">The 1-year crediting period defines the timeframe used to calculate index returns, which are determined annually via the specified formula based on beginning and end-of-period index values.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7898028b-343b-4195-9f4c-a6280a62d640" target="27176921-2e5c-44aa-bcf0-40ddf6e140f2">
  <data key="d3">The 1-year crediting period determines the timeframe used to calculate the index's percentage change, which directly feeds into the computation of credited interest via multiplication by the participation rate.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7898028b-343b-4195-9f4c-a6280a62d640" target="6ff1f4bc-a2b4-4e15-b514-415d803bd39b">
  <data key="d3">The 1-year crediting period defines the timeframe during which interest is calculated under the rules specified in fact_sentence_2, including application of the cap and floor.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7898028b-343b-4195-9f4c-a6280a62d640" target="1b43685f-2a0d-488f-9258-b0a8a87ea9f1">
  <data key="d3">The 1-year crediting period defines the timeframe over which returns are calculated for the Global Diversified Index Account, ensuring that any credited gain aligns with periodic evaluation cycles. This timing does not affect the minimum 4% cap on index-based credits, which remains enforceable irrespective of the period’s length.</data>
  <data key="d4">independently guaranteed</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7898028b-343b-4195-9f4c-a6280a62d640" target="8886f5ce-b28a-43b5-85a1-63104105310a">
  <data key="d3">The 1-year crediting period defines the timeframe over which the interest calculation using a 100% participation rate and 10.5% cap is applied to the Global Diversified Index Account.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7898028b-343b-4195-9f4c-a6280a62d640" target="5af4b2af-c88c-4ee5-ab6b-3214a72b0be8">
  <data key="d3">The 1-year crediting period defines the interval over which index movements are measured; if the index falls by 5% during this period, the floor ensures zero interest is credited, protecting against losses.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7898028b-343b-4195-9f4c-a6280a62d640" target="a7b1c147-442d-4852-b81d-665875dffa47">
  <data key="d3">The 1-year crediting period defines how often performance is calculated for the Global Diversified Index Account, contributing to its structural framework. This periodicity enables the application of safeguards like the 0% floor, preventing negative returns even if markets decline.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
