<edge source="db06e7c6-2f5b-4dca-9e5a-d5dd96d2c405" target="5970ce74-f216-4469-89e2-77ce18166763">
  <data key="d3">The guaranteed 3.0% annual interest rate in the Fixed Account is maintained consistently over time, ensuring predictability for investors.</data>
  <data key="d4">stabilizes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="db06e7c6-2f5b-4dca-9e5a-d5dd96d2c405" target="b24459ef-4087-463c-8274-73d1eef85c9a">
  <data key="d3">The Fixed Account’s guaranteed 3.0% annual return provides stable income, while the lack of a cap allows unlimited upside potential beyond that rate, enhancing long-term value.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="db06e7c6-2f5b-4dca-9e5a-d5dd96d2c405" target="1b43685f-2a0d-488f-9258-b0a8a87ea9f1">
  <data key="d3">The Fixed Account's guaranteed 3% return provides stability, while the 4% minimum cap ensures that even under poor market performance, indexed growth remains meaningful. Together, they reinforce downside protection across account types.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="db06e7c6-2f5b-4dca-9e5a-d5dd96d2c405" target="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7">
  <data key="d3">The guaranteed 3% annual return on the Fixed Account provides a stable benchmark, ensuring investors receive at least that yield regardless of market conditions. This supports the broader framework where even under adverse scenarios, participants benefit from predictable outcomes, complemented by the 25% minimum participation rate in indexed accounts.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="db06e7c6-2f5b-4dca-9e5a-d5dd96d2c405" target="c4dbdf51-a4cd-4a65-8903-f269d529eefd">
  <data key="d3">The fixed account's guaranteed 3.0% annual return is supported by a minimum floor of 2%, ensuring it cannot fall below this level under any circumstances.</data>
  <data key="d4">protects</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="db06e7c6-2f5b-4dca-9e5a-d5dd96d2c405" target="6ff1f4bc-a2b4-4e15-b514-415d803bd39b">
  <data key="d3">The Fixed Account’s guaranteed 3% return aligns with broader protections ensuring interest credits remain within defined bounds; however, unlike indexed accounts, this fixed rate itself isn't typically subject to external caps or participation rates—it remains stable regardless of market fluctuations.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="db06e7c6-2f5b-4dca-9e5a-d5dd96d2c405" target="a7b1c147-442d-4852-b81d-665875dffa47">
  <data key="d3">The guaranteed 3% return in the Fixed Account provides stable growth independent of market movements, contributing to the overall financial security of the product. This stability complements the 0% floor on indexed accounts, ensuring policyholders avoid losses even when markets fall.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="db06e7c6-2f5b-4dca-9e5a-d5dd96d2c405" target="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb">
  <data key="d3">The Fixed Account's 3.0% guaranteed return exceeds the 1% net cost of policy loans, suggesting that utilizing borrowed funds may still yield positive net returns if invested in the Fixed Account.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="db06e7c6-2f5b-4dca-9e5a-d5dd96d2c405" target="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6">
  <data key="d3">The Fixed Account’s 3.0% yield is lower than the 4% loan interest rate, creating a net cost when borrowing against it. This suggests that taking a policy loan may erode the benefits of holding assets in the Fixed Account.</data>
  <data key="d4">economically disadvantageous</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
