<edge source="b5a49b5f-16b1-4dba-94df-96a105e6000e" target="13737585-4de1-4789-b42c-a05bc511593e">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states the percentage invested in the S&amp;P 500 Index, while fact sentence 2 provides information on another component—the NASDAQ-100 Index—in the same portfolio context. Together, they help define the distribution among indexed accounts.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b5a49b5f-16b1-4dba-94df-96a105e6000e" target="122014ab-154e-4331-94fc-e939755b46e6">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 specifies the portion allocated to the S&amp;P 500 Index, while fact sentence 2 indicates the share held in the fixed account. Together, they reflect part of the total portfolio composition under the variable annuity's flexible allocation rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">part of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b5a49b5f-16b1-4dba-94df-96a105e6000e" target="65f18412-1464-4177-ad9f-477c8d9091d3">
  <data key="d3">The current 50% allocation to the S&amp;P 500 reflects investor positioning, while exceeding four annual reallocations triggers a $25 fee, limiting frequent adjustments to such allocations.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b5a49b5f-16b1-4dba-94df-96a105e6000e" target="1b43685f-2a0d-488f-9258-b0a8a87ea9f1">
  <data key="d3">The current allocation to the S&amp;P 500 Index reflects investor positioning within the indexed portion of the account. This allocation operates under a predefined ceiling of 4% for credited returns, ensuring that even if the underlying index performs strongly, returns cannot exceed this limit.</data>
  <data key="d4">constrained by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b5a49b5f-16b1-4dba-94df-96a105e6000e" target="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7">
  <data key="d3">The current allocation to the S&amp;P 500 Index reflects investor positioning within the indexed portion of the account. This allocation operates under a safeguarded framework where participation rates cannot fall below 25%, ensuring consistent upside potential even if market performance varies.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b5a49b5f-16b1-4dba-94df-96a105e6000e" target="665dbf69-ad45-49be-8a49-a811282557e1">
  <data key="d3">The current allocation to the S&amp;P 500 Index reflects investor positioning within the product’s structure. This allocation informs how much of the indexed gain from the S&amp;P 500 is applied when calculating year-end credits based on its percentage change.</data>
  <data key="d4">informs</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b5a49b5f-16b1-4dba-94df-96a105e6000e" target="6ff1f4bc-a2b4-4e15-b514-415d803bd39b">
  <data key="d3">The current allocation to the S&amp;P 500 Index reflects investor positioning within the product’s structure, which operates under rules that limit returns via a cap and protect against loss through a floor.</data>
  <data key="d4">contextualizes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b5a49b5f-16b1-4dba-94df-96a105e6000e" target="27176921-2e5c-44aa-bcf0-40ddf6e140f2">
  <data key="d3">The current 50% allocation to the S&amp;P 500 Index determines the portion of the investor’s funds exposed to its returns, which directly impacts the amount of interest credited under the stated formula.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b5a49b5f-16b1-4dba-94df-96a105e6000e" target="3fe4c74a-f6e1-4f2e-874b-5a03244e9e44">
  <data key="d3">The current allocation of 50% to the S&amp;P 500 Index sets the weight used to calculate overall portfolio exposure. This allocation determines how much impact the index's performance has on total returns if it increases from 4,000 to 4,600.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b5a49b5f-16b1-4dba-94df-96a105e6000e" target="8886f5ce-b28a-43b5-85a1-63104105310a">
  <data key="d3">The current 50% allocation to the S&amp;P 500 Index establishes the basis for applying its performance to calculate potential credits, particularly when combined with specified participation rates and caps.</data>
  <data key="d4">contextual relevance</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b5a49b5f-16b1-4dba-94df-96a105e6000e" target="5af4b2af-c88c-4ee5-ab6b-3214a72b0be8">
  <data key="d3">The current 50% allocation to the S&amp;P 500 Index reflects investor positioning in an indexed account where performance is tied to market movements. In the event of a decline, such as a 5% drop, the 0% floor protects against loss of principal by guaranteeing at least zero interest credit.</data>
  <data key="d4">applies to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b5a49b5f-16b1-4dba-94df-96a105e6000e" target="a7b1c147-442d-4852-b81d-665875dffa47">
  <data key="d3">The S&amp;P 500 Index holds half of the investor's assets, and due to its inclusion in the indexed accounts, it benefits from a 0% floor guarantee that prevents any loss during market downturns.</data>
  <data key="d4">protects</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b5a49b5f-16b1-4dba-94df-96a105e6000e" target="f1ca67d9-884a-4fc4-9ba1-cf7b354e9abd">
  <data key="d3">A 50% allocation to the S&amp;P 500 increases exposure to market volatility, which could lead to lower returns if markets fall sharply. This heightened sensitivity supports the possibility of zero interest being credited when index performance drops significantly.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
