  <data key="d3">Exceeding four annual reallocation requests incurs a $25 fee, potentially affecting how investors manage allocations like the 30% held in the NASDAQ-100 Index.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65f18412-1464-4177-ad9f-477c8d9091d3" target="2b2e3f84-59bf-4a6e-b26c-8b5ae353f6de">
  <data key="d3">Frequent reallocations beyond four per year trigger a $25 fee, thus imposing a cost barrier on exercising the freedom granted by changing allocations on policy anniversaries.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65f18412-1464-4177-ad9f-477c8d9091d3" target="2601679e-fb90-4392-b3a8-8e4aaa913aa1">
  <data key="d3">Each reallocation beyond the initial four per year incurs a $25 fee, except when occurring on a policy anniversary, where it remains free regardless of count.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional exemption</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="65f18412-1464-4177-ad9f-477c8d9091d3" target="6e7acf52-f866-478f-91af-c99f9dc14a24">
  <data key="d3">When more than four reallocation requests occur in a year, a $25 fee applies—this rule only makes sense because the initial four are explicitly stated as free.</data>
  <data key="d4">triggers fee</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
