<edge source="1b43685f-2a0d-488f-9258-b0a8a87ea9f1" target="326a19f6-3d06-4cde-a9f0-0b1923801873">
  <data key="d3">The 4% minimum cap guarantee ensures that even if the Global Diversified Index Account’s cap were to decrease, it would still remain at or above 4%, protecting investors from excessive reductions.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces limit</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1b43685f-2a0d-488f-9258-b0a8a87ea9f1" target="e56d9b1f-113b-4961-abbd-159d8047aeca">
  <data key="d3">Even with a 100% participation rate on the Global Diversified Index, the maximum possible crediting is constrained by the 4% minimum cap rule, ensuring returns do not fall below this level despite strong performance.</data>
  <data key="d4">limits</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1b43685f-2a0d-488f-9258-b0a8a87ea9f1" target="f64306b3-60d7-48b6-82c2-6580397642e1">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that index-based caps never fall below 4% supports investor confidence by ensuring positive returns even in flat markets. This aligns with the 0% floor, creating a dual safeguard against loss and underperformance.</data>
  <data key="d4">enhances</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1b43685f-2a0d-488f-9258-b0a8a87ea9f1" target="7898028b-343b-4195-9f4c-a6280a62d640">
  <data key="d3">A minimum 4% cap on index-based crediting protects investors from inadequate returns, maintaining a baseline level of performance even if market conditions would otherwise yield lower results. This safeguard operates independently of the specific crediting period used, such as the 1-year cycle applied to the Global Diversified Index Account.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditionally applicable</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1b43685f-2a0d-488f-9258-b0a8a87ea9f1" target="db06e7c6-2f5b-4dca-9e5a-d5dd96d2c405">
  <data key="d3">A minimum 4% cap on indexed credits supports long-term attractiveness despite volatility, complementing the Fixed Account’s 3% guaranteed yield by offering upside potential without risking loss.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1b43685f-2a0d-488f-9258-b0a8a87ea9f1" target="b24459ef-4087-463c-8274-73d1eef85c9a">
  <data key="d3">Index-based crediting includes a mandatory minimum cap of 4%, distinguishing it from the uncapped Fixed Account, which offers predictable returns regardless of market conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1b43685f-2a0d-488f-9258-b0a8a87ea9f1" target="b5a49b5f-16b1-4dba-94df-96a105e6000e">
  <data key="d3">A minimum cap of 4% ensures that index-based credits remain bounded above, protecting the insurer from excessive payouts. This constraint applies uniformly across all indexed accounts, including those holding exposure to the S&amp;P 500, thereby influencing potential outcomes of any given allocation like the 50% currently assigned.</data>
  <data key="d4">applies to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1b43685f-2a0d-488f-9258-b0a8a87ea9f1" target="13737585-4de1-4789-b42c-a05bc511593e">
  <data key="d3">A minimum 4% cap on index-based crediting protects investors from poor market outcomes, providing stability regardless of how much is allocated to indices like the NASDAQ-100.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1b43685f-2a0d-488f-9258-b0a8a87ea9f1" target="2b2e3f84-59bf-4a6e-b26c-8b5ae353f6de">
  <data key="d3">The 4% minimum cap on indexed credits provides a safety net for investment decisions made during policy anniversaries, ensuring predictable outcomes despite shifts in asset mix.</data>
  <data key="d4">protects</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1b43685f-2a0d-488f-9258-b0a8a87ea9f1" target="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7">
  <data key="d3">The cap on index-based crediting is set at a minimum of 4%, guaranteeing that even if market gains exceed this level, investors still benefit from a defined upper limit. This ensures stability in potential returns while allowing flexibility within the design parameters.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1b43685f-2a0d-488f-9258-b0a8a87ea9f1" target="665dbf69-ad45-49be-8a49-a811282557e1">
  <data key="d3">The cap ensures that even if the index performs strongly, the credit rate cannot exceed 4%. This limit is applied after calculating the index’s percentage change via the formula described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1b43685f-2a0d-488f-9258-b0a8a87ea9f1" target="27176921-2e5c-44aa-bcf0-40ddf6e140f2">
  <data key="d3">The minimum cap of 4% ensures that even if the index performs strongly, the maximum possible crediting rate cannot exceed this bound when applying the participation rate.</data>
  <data key="d4">constrains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1b43685f-2a0d-488f-9258-b0a8a87ea9f1" target="6ff1f4bc-a2b4-4e15-b514-415d803bd39b">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee that caps will not fall below 4% ensures that even under low-market conditions, the maximum creditable return remains meaningful, directly supporting the broader principle that indexing involves defined upper limits.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1b43685f-2a0d-488f-9258-b0a8a87ea9f1" target="a7b1c147-442d-4852-b81d-665875dffa47">
  <data key="d3">The minimum cap of 4% ensures that while gains are limited, the structural safeguards prevent any loss from market declines, maintaining positive or flat returns regardless of performance.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1b43685f-2a0d-488f-9258-b0a8a87ea9f1" target="8886f5ce-b28a-43b5-85a1-63104105310a">
  <data key="d3">The minimum cap guarantee ensures that even under adverse conditions, index-based returns cannot fall below 4%, providing stability. This constraint allows the illustrative case in fact_sentence_2—where a 10.5% cap applies—to remain valid and meaningful within policy limits.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces limit</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1b43685f-2a0d-488f-9258-b0a8a87ea9f1" target="3fe4c74a-f6e1-4f2e-874b-5a03244e9e44">
  <data key="d3">The minimum cap guarantee ensures that even in scenarios with modest market gains, such as the 15% increase described, the credited return cannot fall below 4%. This rule protects investors while allowing upside exposure based on actual index performance.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1b43685f-2a0d-488f-9258-b0a8a87ea9f1" target="5af4b2af-c88c-4ee5-ab6b-3214a72b0be8">
  <data key="d3">The 4% minimum cap ensures that even under favorable market conditions, the credit rate cannot fall below this level, maintaining predictable upper bounds. This structural limit supports the broader design where market downturns trigger a 0% floor, preserving capital integrity despite volatility.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1b43685f-2a0d-488f-9258-b0a8a87ea9f1" target="f1ca67d9-884a-4fc4-9ba1-cf7b354e9abd">
  <data key="d3">The minimum cap ensures that index-based credits have a defined maximum rate, protecting against excessive volatility. This constraint operates independently from the 0% floor, which prevents negative returns during downturns.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1b43685f-2a0d-488f-9258-b0a8a87ea9f1" target="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a">
  <data key="d3">The 4% minimum cap ensures stable growth in the account value over time, which positively affects the Cash Surrender Value calculation by increasing the base amount before deductions for surrender charges and loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">indirectly affects</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1b43685f-2a0d-488f-9258-b0a8a87ea9f1" target="af34274c-dfee-4fb4-a491-3e2e93de0364">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee that fixed account rates won't fall below minimum levels supports overall financial stability, reinforcing confidence in the product’s reliability even when index-based credits face caps.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1b43685f-2a0d-488f-9258-b0a8a87ea9f1" target="b080d9ad-b053-459f-8150-83b862b99de1">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes a concrete lower bound of 4% for indexing caps, while fact_sentence_2 generalizes this protection by asserting that such caps cannot fall below any guaranteed minimums—confirming the specific figure mentioned earlier.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1b43685f-2a0d-488f-9258-b0a8a87ea9f1" target="a416fa11-2b3f-4f38-958d-ff8e13bcbb1a">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of a minimum 4% cap on indexed credits complements the assurance that participation rates won't drop below their set floors, together reinforcing consistent upside exposure under the product's design.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1b43685f-2a0d-488f-9258-b0a8a87ea9f1" target="05f6ec15-bbb6-4acf-8ed9-90e66f40d069">
  <data key="d3">The 4% minimum cap ensures stable returns even when markets decline, directly supporting the guarantee that policyholders won't suffer losses from negative index performance.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1b43685f-2a0d-488f-9258-b0a8a87ea9f1" target="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a">
  <data key="d3">The 4% minimum cap ensures stable growth in indexed accounts, contributing positively to account value over time. This growing account value impacts the maximum possible death benefit, especially under the Increasing option, where higher values lead to larger benefits. However, outstanding loans reduce the actual payout, potentially offsetting some of the gains accrued via indexing.</data>
  <data key="d4">indirectly affects</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b6d35a57-9072-4e02-9b4b-a2974f7ef7bd" target="1b43685f-2a0d-488f-9258-b0a8a87ea9f1">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">has minimum cap guarantee</data>
</edge>
