<edge source="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7" target="e56d9b1f-113b-4961-abbd-159d8047aeca">
  <data key="d3">The rule requiring participation rates to remain at least 25% ensures that even lower-tier indexes maintain meaningful upside potential; thus, the 100% rate on the Global Diversified Index remains within acceptable bounds.</data>
  <data key="d4">constrains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7" target="f64306b3-60d7-48b6-82c2-6580397642e1">
  <data key="d3">A minimum 25% participation rate ensures meaningful credit accrual when markets rise, working alongside the 0% floor to protect against loss while still enabling positive growth potential in favorable conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">enhances</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7" target="db06e7c6-2f5b-4dca-9e5a-d5dd96d2c405">
  <data key="d3">The 25% minimum participation rate in index-based crediting enhances downside protection by ensuring meaningful upside potential when markets rise, reinforcing confidence alongside the Fixed Account’s guaranteed 3% return, thus maintaining balanced risk management across account types.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7" target="b5a49b5f-16b1-4dba-94df-96a105e6000e">
  <data key="d3">A minimum participation rate of 25% ensures that investors receive at least some benefit from index growth, irrespective of the specific allocation mix. This rule governs how credited returns are computed across all indexed accounts, including those holding exposure to the S&amp;P 500.</data>
  <data key="d4">constrains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7" target="13737585-4de1-4789-b42c-a05bc511593e">
  <data key="d3">A minimum participation rate of 25% applies to all index-based credits, including those tied to the NASDAQ-100. This means any allocation to such indices, like the stated 30%, will benefit from this floor, ensuring non-zero credited growth regardless of negative market movements.</data>
  <data key="d4">contextual support</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7" target="2b2e3f84-59bf-4a6e-b26c-8b5ae353f6de">
  <data key="d3">A guaranteed minimum participation rate of 25% ensures that even if markets perform poorly, investors still receive meaningful credits, supporting strategic rebalancing decisions made at policy anniversaries.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7" target="1b43685f-2a0d-488f-9258-b0a8a87ea9f1">
  <data key="d3">Participation rates are maintained above 25%, meaning investors receive at least a quarter of the index's gain each period. This directly influences how much of the underlying index’s movement translates into credited interest, complementing the cap constraint.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7" target="665dbf69-ad45-49be-8a49-a811282557e1">
  <data key="d3">The participation rate determines what portion of the index’s growth is credited to the investor, based on the index percentage change computed annually per the given formula.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7" target="27176921-2e5c-44aa-bcf0-40ddf6e140f2">
  <data key="d3">The minimum participation rate of 25% ensures that even if the index performs poorly or moderately, the investor still receives at least some positive credit based on the index’s movement, limiting downside exposure while enabling upside potential within cap constraints.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7" target="6ff1f4bc-a2b4-4e15-b514-415d803bd39b">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee that participation rates remain at or above 25% ensures that even under low market performance, investors receive meaningful credit toward their returns, supporting the overall protection offered by the floor and cap system.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7" target="3fe4c74a-f6e1-4f2e-874b-5a03244e9e44">
  <data key="d3">The minimum 25% participation rate ensures that any positive market movement, such as the 15% increase described, results in a proportionally reduced but still positive credited return. This cap on participation limits upside exposure while guaranteeing non-negative outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7" target="a7b1c147-442d-4852-b81d-665875dffa47">
  <data key="d3">The minimum 25% participation rate ensures that even when market performance is weak, the policyholder still receives meaningful credits, contributing to the overall protection from negative returns during market declines.</data>
  <data key="d4">enhances</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7" target="5af4b2af-c88c-4ee5-ab6b-3214a72b0be8">
  <data key="d3">The 25% minimum participation rate ensures meaningful upside capture if the index rises, while the 0% floor prevents any loss if the index falls by 5%. Together, they create a balanced incentive structure within the indexed accounts.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7" target="8886f5ce-b28a-43b5-85a1-63104105310a">
  <data key="d3">The minimum 25% participation rate ensures that even in low-return scenarios, investors receive some benefit from index growth. This baseline allows higher participation rates like 100% to fully leverage index performance within the cap limit.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional dependency</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7" target="f1ca67d9-884a-4fc4-9ba1-cf7b354e9abd">
  <data key="d3">A minimum participation rate of 25% ensures that even in declining markets, the policyholder receives at least partial indexing benefit, preventing total loss despite negative market performance.</data>
  <data key="d4">protects against</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7" target="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a">
  <data key="d3">The minimum 25% participation rate ensures that indexed account growth contributes positively to the overall account value, which directly impacts the Cash Surrender Value calculation described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7" target="b080d9ad-b053-459f-8150-83b862b99de1">
  <data key="d3">The guaranteed minimum participation rate of 25% supports stable crediting even when cap rates are low, reinforcing the overall safety net provided by the rule that cap rates cannot fall below minimums.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7" target="a416fa11-2b3f-4f38-958d-ff8e13bcbb1a">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 provides a concrete example of a guaranteed minimum (25%) for participation rates, which supports and exemplifies the more general claim in fact_sentence_2 about rate floors being enforced.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7" target="af34274c-dfee-4fb4-a491-3e2e93de0364">
  <data key="d3">The minimum 25% participation rate for indexed accounts complements the assurance that fixed account rates won't fall below guaranteed levels, reinforcing overall stability and predictable returns regardless of market conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
