  <data key="d3">Even if market performance leads to zero credits due to declines, policyholders retain full control through periodic reallocations, enabling proactive adjustments to mitigate future risks or shift toward more stable assets like the fixed account.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f1ca67d9-884a-4fc4-9ba1-cf7b354e9abd" target="2601679e-fb90-4392-b3a8-8e4aaa913aa1">
  <data key="d3">The 0% floor protects investors from losing value during market drops, making it safer to make frequent allocation shifts. Since such changes incur no cost on policy anniversaries, holders can realign portfolios without penalty, enhancing control over risk exposure.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables flexibility</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f1ca67d9-884a-4fc4-9ba1-cf7b354e9abd" target="6e7acf52-f866-478f-91af-c99f9dc14a24">
  <data key="d3">Even in severe market declines, the 0% floor prevents any loss of credited interest, making it safe to use the available free reallocations to shift assets without fear of compounding losses.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
