<edge source="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299" target="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db">
  <data key="d3">A floor protection level of 0% means that even if the index falls by up to 5%, the policyholder’s account value cannot go below zero, thus ensuring no loss as stated in the first fact.</data>
  <data key="d4">sets threshold</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299" target="70667dae-ff8c-4bac-bf04-03807ddb6bd7">
  <data key="d3">The floor protection level being 0% ensures that the policyholder’s account value cannot drop below zero during market downturns, preventing any loss of principal regardless of how much the underlying index falls.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299" target="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1">
  <data key="d3">The 0% floor protection means the policyholder cannot lose money due to market losses, resulting in a minimum return of 0%. This directly leads to the worst-case scenario where the policyholder earns exactly 0% interest over the year.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299" target="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7">
  <data key="d3">The floor protection level being 0% means the account value is safeguarded from declining below zero, ensuring that even during a 5% index drop, the account does not lose value. This results in 0% interest credited, reflecting the protective cap on downside risk.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299" target="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176">
  <data key="d3">Floor protection at 0% ensures the policyholder’s account value won’t drop below zero during market downturns, providing financial safety net regardless of performance. This safeguard remains effective only if premiums meet the minimum threshold of $100, ensuring continued participation in the policy's protections.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299" target="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e">
  <data key="d3">Floor protection at 0% prevents the account value from declining further during market downturns, ensuring it remains viable to meet future monthly charges even when premiums aren't paid.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299" target="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d">
  <data key="d3">The floor protection mechanism prevents losses during market downturns, ensuring stability in the policy’s value. This stability helps support long-term viability, enabling the recommended $6,000 annual premium to effectively sustain coverage through retirement.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299" target="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae">
  <data key="d3">The zero-floor protection ensures the policy’s value won’t drop below its initial or minimum threshold during market downturns. This stability supports the ability to maintain sufficient account value over time, enabling future skipping of premiums without lapsing coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299" target="2bf05a03-d336-46dd-a382-121bb038f1a6">
  <data key="d3">The floor protection being set at 0% ensures downside risk is fully mitigated regardless of market performance. This structural safeguard provides stability upon which long-term financial planning—including the recommended $6,000 annual contribution—is based.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299" target="9639c325-d6a7-4181-a801-0a4fdfaefa94">
  <data key="d3">Floor protection prevents the account value from falling below zero during market downturns, ensuring stability. This stable baseline affects how the cost-of-insurance charge is calculated, since the COI deduction relies on the current account value compared to the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299" target="e2637b0a-dd20-4e01-8fa1-8779d2f346fa">
  <data key="d3">Floor protection at 0% ensures the account value remains stable despite market losses, providing downside safety. This complements the guarantee on COI rates, ensuring that ongoing insurance expenses remain fixed over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299" target="eec22563-c8f9-4930-abc2-6252103b7b77">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 states the floor protection is set at 0%, which directly corresponds to fact_sentence_1’s definition of the Floor Rate as the minimum crediting rate, confirming consistency in risk mitigation design.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299" target="faf66c9e-da0e-4813-9561-2d1480419596">
  <data key="d3">A 0% floor protects the account from negative returns, making the 100% participation rate meaningful since any positive movement in the S&amp;P 500 is fully captured without fear of erosion from market drops.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299" target="42ce1796-4b22-4fa1-987f-341d1746d7f3">
  <data key="d3">A 0% floor protects against market decline, consistent with the design of the Point-to-Point Method’s annual interest crediting system.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299" target="f64306b3-60d7-48b6-82c2-6580397642e1">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 states a 0% floor for a life insurance policy’s account value, matching the guarantee mentioned in fact_sentence_1 about the Global Diversified Index Account, reinforcing common protective mechanisms despite differing product types.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299" target="a7b1c147-442d-4852-b81d-665875dffa47">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 establishes a 0% floor protection level, which directly explains why fact_sentence_1 claims market declines cannot cause negative returns for the policyholder.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299" target="f1ca67d9-884a-4fc4-9ba1-cf7b354e9abd">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 states that the policy includes a 0% floor protecting against market downturns, reinforcing the same principle found in fact_sentence_1, where the annuity’s design prevents any reduction below zero interest due to market performance.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299" target="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb">
  <data key="d3">The absence of floor protection increases vulnerability to market declines, but the very low net cost of policy loans provides a financially viable mechanism to access funds without significant penalty during downturns.</data>
  <data key="d4">complemented by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299" target="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22">
  <data key="d3">A lack of floor protection means the policy’s account value could decline significantly, potentially impacting the ability to repay loans taken at a 4% rate, despite the loan growing at 3% in the fixed account.</data>
  <data key="d4">increases risk</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.68</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299" target="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a">
  <data key="d3">Without any floor protection, the policyholder’s account value is fully exposed to market volatility, making it more likely that accumulated loans will significantly deplete the remaining balance before death, thereby reducing the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">exacerbates risk</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299" target="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9">
  <data key="d3">A 0% floor means the account has no protection against losses, so large or frequent partial withdrawals may deplete funds faster, particularly if the investment performs poorly. This makes adherence to the $500 minimum withdrawal threshold more risky over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">increases risk</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.68</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299" target="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5">
  <data key="d3">The lack of floor protection means the account value can decline without limit, making it more susceptible to being reduced by recurring fees such as the $50 charge applied to partial withdrawals after the tenth year.</data>
  <data key="d4">compounds risk</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b3c80b37-b6dd-4ee3-848c-41ccb8525526" target="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">has protection level</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7a31a069-cacc-4e50-8f53-44e40bed808e" target="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">has floor protection level</data>
</edge>
