<edge source="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7" target="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db">
  <data key="d3">A 5% drop in the index triggers zero interest crediting, which aligns with the floor protection feature designed to prevent losses during such market declines.</data>
  <data key="d4">result of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7" target="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299">
  <data key="d3">When the index falls by 5%, the policy credits 0% interest to prevent any loss, which reflects the implementation of the 0% floor protection level designed to guarantee minimum account value stability.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7" target="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1">
  <data key="d3">If the index falls by 5%, the account receives no interest credit, resulting in a zero percent return for the year—a situation representing the worst possible performance.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7" target="70667dae-ff8c-4bac-bf04-03807ddb6bd7">
  <data key="d3">If the index falls by 5%, no interest is credited to the account, ensuring that the principal remains intact and preventing any financial loss.</data>
  <data key="d4">ensures protection</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7" target="50dee1d7-a696-448d-92e6-11dfe14d068f">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of 0% interest on account value during a 5% index drop ensures financial stability regardless of market conditions. This protective mechanism complements the policy’s flexible premium payments, allowing consistent contributions without fear of losing gains due to volatility.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7" target="86b72d75-5a59-44c2-b2d6-912ce393cf76">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of no negative interest during a 5% index decline ensures financial safety regardless of market conditions. This protection operates independently of when premiums are paid, supporting consistent account integrity across flexible payment schedules.</data>
  <data key="d4">independently supports</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7" target="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of zero interest on a 5% drop in the index ensures stability in the account's growth potential, which supports long-term sustainability. This feature indirectly reinforces why consistent contributions—even minimal ones like $100—are necessary to preserve the policy’s benefits over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7" target="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee that no losses occur when the index falls by 5% ensures account value preservation, indirectly supporting sustained ability to meet the recommended $6,000 annual premium over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7" target="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e">
  <data key="d3">The guaranteed minimum interest rate ensures stability during market downturns, preserving account value needed to cover future monthly charges. This preserved value enables flexibility in paying premiums or skipping them altogether.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7" target="2bf05a03-d336-46dd-a382-121bb038f1a6">
  <data key="d3">The guaranteed floor at 0% interest during a 5% drop ensures stable performance under stress scenarios, supporting the long-term viability of the recommended contribution plan based on projected actuarial outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7" target="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of zero interest during a 5% index drop ensures account value resilience, helping maintain funds needed to cover monthly charges and enabling potential premium skips under certain conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">indirectly supports</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7" target="6c580dbf-ec5e-4009-845b-7efb65de3c5a">
  <data key="d3">A 5% decline in the index triggers a zero interest crediting rule, safeguarding the account balance. This protective mechanism helps maintain policy integrity, potentially reducing strain on administrative systems funded by the premium load.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7" target="e2637b0a-dd20-4e01-8fa1-8779d2f346fa">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of zero interest on a 5% index decline provides downside protection, stabilizing account value. This complements the assurance that COI rates won’t rise above set limits, contributing collectively to long-term financial predictability.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7" target="eec22563-c8f9-4930-abc2-6252103b7b77">
  <data key="d3">A 5% decline leading to 0% interest credits demonstrates the practical effect of the 0% Floor Rate, confirming its role in risk mitigation.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7" target="faf66c9e-da0e-4813-9561-2d1480419596">
  <data key="d3">The absence of interest credit during a 5% drop supports the presence of a 0% floor, which complements the 100% Participation Rate described in the first statement.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7" target="42ce1796-4b22-4fa1-987f-341d1746d7f3">
  <data key="d3">A 0% floor rate under the Point-to-Point Method guarantees that declining indices do not reduce account value, justifying why interest remains at 0% after a 5% decline.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7" target="f64306b3-60d7-48b6-82c2-6580397642e1">
  <data key="d3">A 5% decline leading to 0% credited interest reflects the same principle as the 0% floor mentioned in fact_sentence_1, suggesting consistent downside protection across products.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7" target="a7b1c147-442d-4852-b81d-665875dffa47">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 describes a scenario where a 5% decline leads to 0% credited interest, which exemplifies and supports fact_sentence_1's broader claim about protection from negative returns during market declines.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7" target="f1ca67d9-884a-4fc4-9ba1-cf7b354e9abd">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 demonstrates a real-world application where a 5% market decline leads to zero interest credited—a condition explicitly supported by the 0% floor feature detailed in chunk_summary_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7" target="6c81117f-d67b-45c8-b7c8-8a2a822df46d">
  <data key="d3">The absence of interest credit on market decline ensures capital preservation, which complements the ability to make early partial withdrawals without fees, enhancing financial flexibility during volatile periods.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="507305a8-fc58-439f-9416-e6b4a4698e9b" target="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">provides protection against</data>
</edge>
