<edge source="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1" target="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db">
  <data key="d3">The worst possible outcome—earning 0% interest—is made possible because the policy includes floor protection preventing any negative returns during market downturns.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1" target="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299">
  <data key="d3">If the worst-case scenario occurs—earning 0% interest—it confirms the effectiveness of the 0% floor protection, which prevents any decline in the account value despite adverse market conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1" target="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7">
  <data key="d3">Earning 0% interest for the year occurs specifically when the index decline reaches or exceeds 5%, triggering the floor on interest crediting.</data>
  <data key="d4">condition for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1" target="70667dae-ff8c-4bac-bf04-03807ddb6bd7">
  <data key="d3">Since the policyholder cannot lose money due to market downturns, the maximum downside risk is capped at earning nothing—an outcome consistent with the principle described in the prior statement about guaranteed protection.</data>
  <data key="d4">follows from</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1" target="2bf05a03-d336-46dd-a382-121bb038f1a6">
  <data key="d3">The worst-case scenario of earning 0% interest hinges on the accuracy of the underlying actuarial and financial assumptions used to model risk and returns.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1" target="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d">
  <data key="d3">A 0% interest rate represents a significant risk to policy sustainability; contributing $6,000 annually helps offset such losses and ensures continued coverage through age 100 despite poor performance.</data>
  <data key="d4">mitigates risk</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1" target="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e">
  <data key="d3">If the policyholder earns 0% interest, the account value grows minimally or stagnates, making it harder to maintain sufficient funds to cover monthly charges without additional contributions.</data>
  <data key="d4">inhibits</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1" target="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae">
  <data key="d3">If the policy earns 0% interest, the account value remains stagnant, increasing reliance on existing balances to cover ongoing costs. This makes it more likely that skipped premiums can still be tolerated as long as the account holds enough to absorb monthly fees.</data>
  <data key="d4">enhances risk mitigation</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.78</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1" target="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d">
  <data key="d3">If the policyholder pays premiums subject to a 3.5% load, less money is allocated to the account value, increasing the chance that the investment earns 0% interest over the year due to fees eroding gains.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1" target="9639c325-d6a7-4181-a801-0a4fdfaefa94">
  <data key="d3">A zero-interest scenario impacts overall account growth, indirectly affecting the account value over time, which influences the basis for calculating monthly COI deductions tied to the difference between the death benefit and account value.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1" target="eec22563-c8f9-4930-abc2-6252103b7b77">
  <data key="d3">The worst-case scenario of earning 0% interest corresponds exactly to the Floor Rate's function, confirming that the 0% floor prevents any downside risk from market losses.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1" target="faf66c9e-da0e-4813-9561-2d1480419596">
  <data key="d3">The assurance of earning at least 0% interest under adverse conditions is consistent with the 0% floor rate implied by the 100% Participation Rate on the S&amp;P 500 Index Account.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1" target="42ce1796-4b22-4fa1-987f-341d1746d7f3">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of earning at least 0% interest stems directly from the 0% floor embedded in the Point-to-Point Method’s design, making it consistent with the stated risk mitigation.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
