  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">date</data>
</edge>
<edge source="50dee1d7-a696-448d-92e6-11dfe14d068f" target="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7">
  <data key="d3">Flexible premium payments enable ongoing funding of the policy, supporting sustained participation in the indexed account where the 0% floor applies during a 5% index decline. The availability of timely payments helps maintain the integrity of the downside protection feature.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="50dee1d7-a696-448d-92e6-11dfe14d068f" target="70667dae-ff8c-4bac-bf04-03807ddb6bd7">
  <data key="d3">Flexible premium payment timing allows policyholders to contribute funds when convenient, reinforcing trust in the product’s stability despite market fluctuations.</data>
  <data key="d4">supports risk tolerance</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="50dee1d7-a696-448d-92e6-11dfe14d068f" target="86b72d75-5a59-44c2-b2d6-912ce393cf76">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states that premiums can be paid at any time, which directly supports and reinforces the idea presented in fact sentence 2—that there are no restrictions on when payments can occur.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="50dee1d7-a696-448d-92e6-11dfe14d068f" target="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa">
  <data key="d3">The ability to pay premiums at any time allows policyholders to make contributions whenever convenient, subject to a minimum threshold of $100 per payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">flexibility with limit</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="50dee1d7-a696-448d-92e6-11dfe14d068f" target="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176">
  <data key="d3">The statement that premiums can be paid at any time sets the temporal framework for contributions, but this flexibility is constrained by the requirement that each payment must meet a minimum threshold of $100.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="50dee1d7-a696-448d-92e6-11dfe14d068f" target="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2">
  <data key="d3">The statement that premiums can be paid at any time establishes temporal flexibility, which operates under the constraint defined by the maximum allowable annual payment of $50,000.</data>
  <data key="d4">flexibility with limit</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="50dee1d7-a696-448d-92e6-11dfe14d068f" target="0d35c1ce-d96d-4562-80f8-0654abe126d2">
  <data key="d3">The ability to pay premiums at any time reflects flexible scheduling, while the $50,000 annual cap ensures compliance with IRS tax qualifications, establishing a legal boundary for contributions.</data>
  <data key="d4">conforms to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="50dee1d7-a696-448d-92e6-11dfe14d068f" target="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d">
  <data key="d3">The ability to pay premiums at any time enables policyholders to meet the recommended annual contribution of $6,000 when convenient, supporting sustained coverage through flexible scheduling.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="50dee1d7-a696-448d-92e6-11dfe14d068f" target="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae">
  <data key="d3">The ability to pay premiums at any time enables policyholders to maintain funding levels necessary to cover future costs, allowing them to skip payments when the account balance suffices.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="50dee1d7-a696-448d-92e6-11dfe14d068f" target="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e">
  <data key="d3">The flexibility to pay premiums at any time depends on having adequate account value to absorb monthly charges without triggering lapses or penalties.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="50dee1d7-a696-448d-92e6-11dfe14d068f" target="2bf05a03-d336-46dd-a382-121bb038f1a6">
  <data key="d3">The ability to pay premiums at any time allows policyholders to align contributions with personal finances, though sustaining long-term coverage relies on consistent payments under unchanged actuarial and financial assumptions.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="50dee1d7-a696-448d-92e6-11dfe14d068f" target="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d">
  <data key="d3">The ability to pay premiums at any time enables the application of a uniform 3.5% load on every payment, ensuring consistency in how fees are assessed over variable payment schedules.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="50dee1d7-a696-448d-92e6-11dfe14d068f" target="1b6d4d68-07ed-4c80-987c-ddf958d36f08">
  <data key="d3">The ability to pay premiums at any time allows policyholders to make contributions before the monthly deduction date, potentially influencing how much is left in the account after charges are taken.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="50dee1d7-a696-448d-92e6-11dfe14d068f" target="0b7e0a06-5166-489d-a873-3b798f915e2c">
  <data key="d3">The flexibility to pay premiums at any time enables ongoing funding of the policy, which supports the sustained deduction of monthly charges like COI and administrative fees from the account balance.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
