<edge source="86b72d75-5a59-44c2-b2d6-912ce393cf76" target="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7">
  <data key="d3">Flexible premium payment timing allows contributors to adjust deposits without constraints, enabling them to maintain coverage under any schedule. This freedom complements the policy’s built-in floor mechanism, which prevents losses due to market volatility.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables stability</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="86b72d75-5a59-44c2-b2d6-912ce393cf76" target="50dee1d7-a696-448d-92e6-11dfe14d068f">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 clarifies that there is no limitation on the timing of premium payments, reinforcing the claim made in fact sentence 1 that such payments can be made at any time.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="86b72d75-5a59-44c2-b2d6-912ce393cf76" target="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176">
  <data key="d3">The absence of time restrictions on premium payments allows policyholders to pay whenever convenient, as long as each payment meets the minimum threshold of $100.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="86b72d75-5a59-44c2-b2d6-912ce393cf76" target="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa">
  <data key="d3">The absence of timing restrictions allows policyholders to pay premiums at any point, enabling them to meet the mandatory minimum of $100 whenever convenient.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="86b72d75-5a59-44c2-b2d6-912ce393cf76" target="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2">
  <data key="d3">The absence of timing restrictions allows policyholders to make premium payments at any point during the year, enabling them to reach the upper annual limit of $50,000 whenever convenient.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="86b72d75-5a59-44c2-b2d6-912ce393cf76" target="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d">
  <data key="d3">The lack of timing restrictions allows individuals to pay premiums at any point during the year, facilitating the ability to meet the recommended $6,000 annual contribution consistently.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="86b72d75-5a59-44c2-b2d6-912ce393cf76" target="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae">
  <data key="d3">The absence of timing restrictions allows policyholders to defer payments, enabling them to skip contributions if their account balance remains adequate to absorb monthly charges without lapsing.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="86b72d75-5a59-44c2-b2d6-912ce393cf76" target="2bf05a03-d336-46dd-a382-121bb038f1a6">
  <data key="d3">The absence of restrictions on premium payment timing allows policyholders flexibility, but the effectiveness of the recommended $6,000 annual contribution hinges on sustained actuarial and financial assumptions.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="86b72d75-5a59-44c2-b2d6-912ce393cf76" target="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e">
  <data key="d3">The absence of restrictions on when premiums can be paid allows policyholders flexibility, enabling them to skip payments only if the account has enough value to absorb monthly charges like cost-of-insurance and admin fees.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="86b72d75-5a59-44c2-b2d6-912ce393cf76" target="e2637b0a-dd20-4e01-8fa1-8779d2f346fa">
  <data key="d3">The flexible timing of premium payments allows policyholders to contribute funds at any point during the year, supporting sustained funding needed to maintain coverage under the guaranteed COI rates.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
