<edge source="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa" target="70667dae-ff8c-4bac-bf04-03807ddb6bd7">
  <data key="d3">The minimum premium of $100 per payment enables continued participation in the policy, supporting its core promise of protecting principal during market downturns.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables protection</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa" target="50dee1d7-a696-448d-92e6-11dfe14d068f">
  <data key="d3">A mandatory minimum payment of $100 ensures that every premium installment meets a baseline requirement, regardless of when it is made during the year.</data>
  <data key="d4">constraint on timing</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa" target="86b72d75-5a59-44c2-b2d6-912ce393cf76">
  <data key="d3">A required minimum payment of $100 ensures that every premium installment, regardless of when it's made, meets a baseline financial commitment under the policy.</data>
  <data key="d4">enforces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa" target="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 restates the minimum payment threshold already mentioned in fact_sentence_1, providing redundancy for clarity.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">1.0</data>
</edge>
<edge source="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa" target="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 sets the floor at $100 per payment, ensuring minimal contributions are accepted. Fact_sentence_2 caps total annual payments at $50,000, defining the ceiling for premium flexibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">complementary limits</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa" target="0d35c1ce-d96d-4562-80f8-0654abe126d2">
  <data key="d3">The $100 minimum premium sets a floor for contributions, ensuring basic participation, while the $50,000 annual ceiling ensures compliance with federal tax regulations governing qualified plans.</data>
  <data key="d4">compliance limit</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa" target="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d">
  <data key="d3">The minimum $100 annual premium sets a floor for contributions, below which coverage may not be maintained; however, the recommended $6,000 ensures sustained benefits through age 100 by providing adequate funding over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa" target="2bf05a03-d336-46dd-a382-121bb038f1a6">
  <data key="d3">The minimum premium of $100 sets a floor for contributions, but its effectiveness in sustaining coverage relies on broader actuarial and financial conditions assumed in the recommendation.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa" target="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae">
  <data key="d3">The minimum payment requirement sets a baseline for contributing funds, ensuring financial stability within the policy; however, skipping payments remains possible if the accumulated account value exceeds required deductions.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa" target="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e">
  <data key="d3">The minimum premium of $100 sets the baseline for contributions; ensuring the account holds enough value to absorb monthly fees allows policyholders to potentially skip future payments without lapsing coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa" target="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d">
  <data key="d3">The minimum premium of $100 sets the baseline for contributions, upon which a 3.5% load is calculated. This means that at least part of the $100 is absorbed by the loading fee regardless of the chosen amount within the range.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa" target="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f">
  <data key="d3">The $100 minimum premium sets the baseline for funding, ensuring sufficient capital remains after monthly deductions like Cost of Insurance (COI). This ensures the policy stays active despite recurring fees.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa" target="6c580dbf-ec5e-4009-845b-7efb65de3c5a">
  <data key="d3">The minimum premium of $100 ensures that enough funds enter the system to support the 3.5% load, which covers administrative and operational costs. Without such a threshold, the load could deplete the account too quickly.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa" target="749f8b25-e9c6-4e2e-a60a-5fdcef1215c4">
  <data key="d3">The minimum premium of $100 ensures consistent funding into the policy, which affects the account value over time. This account value is a key variable in determining the monthly COI charge via the given formula.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa" target="a7b1c147-442d-4852-b81d-665875dffa47">
  <data key="d3">Meeting the $100 minimum premium enables enrollment in the policy’s risk-mitigated investment framework, where market declines cannot cause losses due to built-in floors.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables protection</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa" target="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e">
  <data key="d3">The $100 minimum premium ensures sustained funding necessary to avoid lapses, making it more likely that surrender charges would apply if the policy were terminated prematurely due to non-payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa" target="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018">
  <data key="d3">The minimum premium requirement ensures sufficient funding to support the policy's longevity, directly influencing whether a policyholder may face significant surrender charges if they terminate coverage early due to insufficient contributions.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa" target="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890">
  <data key="d3">The minimum premium requirement ensures sufficient contributions to support long-term policy maintenance, indirectly affecting when and how much a policyholder might face surrender charges like the 9% in Year 2 if they withdraw funds prematurely.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa" target="00111295-2bb8-4547-912d-c65ce0d8d633">
  <data key="d3">The minimum premium requirement ensures adequate funding to support long-term policy maintenance, influencing whether the policyholder might face surrender charges like the 6% fee in Year 5 due to early withdrawal.</data>
  <data key="d4">contextual relationship</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa" target="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73">
  <data key="d3">The $100 minimum premium supports long-term policy sustainability, enabling the holder to eventually access full benefits without surrender fees after Year 12.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa" target="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df">
  <data key="d3">The $100 minimum premium ensures eligibility for ongoing coverage, influencing the calculation of surrender charges based on total premiums paid in the initial decade.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa" target="a3cf559b-392a-434d-8391-67212bc086c3">
  <data key="d3">The $100 minimum premium ensures ongoing policy funding, which contributes to building account value over time. This accumulated value influences the magnitude of surrender charges, such as the 1% fee in Year 10, making sustained payments relevant to minimizing future exit costs.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa" target="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a">
  <data key="d3">The minimum premium of $100 contributes to building the account value, which is a key factor in calculating the cash surrender value described in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa" target="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86">
  <data key="d3">The $100 minimum premium ensures ongoing policy viability, enabling the holder to remain within the term when surrender charges like the 0.5% in Year 11 still apply. Consistent payments help avoid lapses and support eligibility for lower future surrender fees.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
