<edge source="2bf05a03-d336-46dd-a382-121bb038f1a6" target="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db">
  <data key="d3">The recommended contribution depends on stable actuarial assumptions, which are reinforced by the presence of downside protection mechanisms like the 5% floor.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2bf05a03-d336-46dd-a382-121bb038f1a6" target="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299">
  <data key="d3">The recommendation to contribute $6,000 annually relies on stable actuarial and financial assumptions, ensuring sustainability of benefits up to age 100. These assumptions support the viability of maintaining coverage despite the absence of negative returns due to the 0% floor protection.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2bf05a03-d336-46dd-a382-121bb038f1a6" target="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7">
  <data key="d3">The recommended $6,000 annual contribution relies on sustained favorable actuarial projections; without such assumptions, the safety net described in the first statement may still apply regardless of funding levels.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2bf05a03-d336-46dd-a382-121bb038f1a6" target="70667dae-ff8c-4bac-bf04-03807ddb6bd7">
  <data key="d3">The assumption that current actuarial and financial conditions hold true justifies the confidence in maintaining principal value despite market volatility, reinforcing the effectiveness of the protective feature.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2bf05a03-d336-46dd-a382-121bb038f1a6" target="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1">
  <data key="d3">The assumption that current actuarial and financial models hold true directly informs the assessment of what constitutes a worst-case outcome like 0% interest.</data>
  <data key="d4">underlies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2bf05a03-d336-46dd-a382-121bb038f1a6" target="50dee1d7-a696-448d-92e6-11dfe14d068f">
  <data key="d3">Recommendations such as contributing $6,000 annually assume ongoing favorable actuarial and financial conditions; without them, timely premium payments may not suffice to maintain coverage despite their flexibility.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2bf05a03-d336-46dd-a382-121bb038f1a6" target="86b72d75-5a59-44c2-b2d6-912ce393cf76">
  <data key="d3">While the recommendation assumes consistent actuarial and financial conditions, it does not override the lack of constraints on when premiums may be paid.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2bf05a03-d336-46dd-a382-121bb038f1a6" target="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176">
  <data key="d3">The assumption behind the $6,000 recommendation relies on current actuarial models, meaning its sustainability hinges on meeting the minimum $100 premium requirement to maintain policy integrity.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2bf05a03-d336-46dd-a382-121bb038f1a6" target="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa">
  <data key="d3">The recommendation's validity hinges on stable actuarial and financial assumptions, which ensure that even minimal payments like $100 contribute meaningfully toward lifelong coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2bf05a03-d336-46dd-a382-121bb038f1a6" target="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 indicates that the suggested $6,000 contribution relies on existing assumptions, which contextualizes the significance of the $50,000 annual ceiling mentioned in fact_sentence_1—suggesting such caps could also be assumption-dependent.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2bf05a03-d336-46dd-a382-121bb038f1a6" target="0d35c1ce-d96d-4562-80f8-0654abe126d2">
  <data key="d3">The recommendation of a $6,000 annual contribution depends on prevailing actuarial and financial assumptions, which are constrained by external factors such as the $50,000 tax-qualified premium cap.</data>
  <data key="d4">boundary</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2bf05a03-d336-46dd-a382-121bb038f1a6" target="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d">
  <data key="d3">The assumption of current actuarial and financial stability underpins the viability of maintaining coverage through a $6,000 annual premium.</data>
  <data key="d4">justifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2bf05a03-d336-46dd-a382-121bb038f1a6" target="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae">
  <data key="d3">The assumption behind the recommended contribution level affects whether skipped premiums remain viable, as it determines if the account balance can cover ongoing fees without additional funding.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2bf05a03-d336-46dd-a382-121bb038f1a6" target="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e">
  <data key="d3">The recommendation about flexible premium contributions depends on stable actuarial and financial assumptions; however, such flexibility requires sufficient account value to absorb monthly fees without triggering lapses.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2bf05a03-d336-46dd-a382-121bb038f1a6" target="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d">
  <data key="d3">The recommendation relies on stable actuarial conditions, which may be affected by fees like the 3.5% premium load that reduce net contributions to the policy’s growth.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2bf05a03-d336-46dd-a382-121bb038f1a6" target="6c580dbf-ec5e-4009-845b-7efb65de3c5a">
  <data key="d3">The recommendation for contributing $6,000 annually depends on maintained actuarial and financial stability, which ensures long-term viability. This assumption indirectly supports the justification for applying a fixed premium load, as consistent funding models underpin expense coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2bf05a03-d336-46dd-a382-121bb038f1a6" target="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f">
  <data key="d3">The recommendation relies on consistent financial modeling, which includes predictable expenses like the monthly Cost of Insurance deduction. Without regular COI deductions being applied as assumed, the projected sustainability could fail.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="2bf05a03-d336-46dd-a382-121bb038f1a6" target="e2637b0a-dd20-4e01-8fa1-8779d2f346fa">
  <data key="d3">The assurance that COI rates won’t exceed policy-specified levels strengthens confidence in the sustainability of the recommended contribution plan, validating its reliance on stable financial assumptions.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="501c88bd-10d5-4b96-8ea0-02244e633f04" target="2bf05a03-d336-46dd-a382-121bb038f1a6">
