</edge>
<edge source="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae" target="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db">
  <data key="d3">The ability to skip premium payments relies on having enough account value after deducting monthly charges. Maintaining adequate value is supported by floor protection, which safeguards gains during downturns.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae" target="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299">
  <data key="d3">If the account value is high enough to absorb ongoing monthly charges, policyholders can pause premium contributions. This financial buffer helps preserve the policy's integrity, especially when combined with built-in floor protections like the 0% guarantee.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae" target="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7">
  <data key="d3">If the account value remains high enough to absorb monthly deductions—including cost-of-insurance and admin fees—it increases the likelihood that the policyholder can avoid paying premiums, thereby benefiting from the built-in 5% market decline protection.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables safety net</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae" target="70667dae-ff8c-4bac-bf04-03807ddb6bd7">
  <data key="d3">The ability to skip premium payments relies on having enough account value to absorb monthly charges; this feasibility is supported by the policy’s protection against market-driven losses, preserving the account balance over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae" target="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1">
  <data key="d3">The ability to skip premium payments depends on having sufficient account value to offset monthly charges; without positive growth or contributions, maintaining such reserves becomes harder when interest earnings are zero.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on account value</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.78</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae" target="50dee1d7-a696-448d-92e6-11dfe14d068f">
  <data key="d3">If a policyholder skips a premium payment, it implies they rely on accumulated account value; thus, the option to delay payments depends on having previously contributed via flexible premium schedules.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae" target="86b72d75-5a59-44c2-b2d6-912ce393cf76">
  <data key="d3">Flexible payment timing permits skipped payments only when the account has enough value to withstand deductions, reinforcing the practical application of payment freedom.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae" target="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176">
  <data key="d3">If a policyholder has maintained enough account value through prior payments meeting the $100 minimum, they may choose to skip current premiums without immediate risk of lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae" target="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa">
  <data key="d3">Even though premiums can be skipped when the account has enough value to absorb fees, maintaining at least the minimum $100 payment helps preserve long-term sustainability and avoids depletion risks.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables sustainability</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae" target="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2">
  <data key="d3">If the account value remains high due to consistent or large contributions up to the $50,000 annual limit, policyholders gain the option to skip payments without lapsing coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae" target="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d">
  <data key="d3">If the account value suffices to cover monthly charges without additional premiums, then maintaining the recommended $6,000 annual contribution becomes optional, though still advisable for longevity.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae" target="2bf05a03-d336-46dd-a382-121bb038f1a6">
  <data key="d3">If the account value remains sufficient to absorb monthly charges despite missed payments, the underlying actuarial and financial assumptions supporting the recommendation are validated or at least plausible.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae" target="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e">
  <data key="d3">Skipping premium payments depends on having enough account value to cover ongoing monthly fees. This ensures financial sustainability without active contributions.</data>
  <data key="d4">condition required</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae" target="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d">
  <data key="d3">The ability to skip payments relies on having enough account value, which could be impacted by the 3.5% load that reduces the effective growth per payment. However, the load itself does not determine eligibility for skipping payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae" target="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f">
  <data key="d3">If the account value is sufficient to cover monthly deductions—including Cost of Insurance—the policyholder may skip paying premiums. This ensures continued coverage despite non-payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional dependency</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae" target="6c580dbf-ec5e-4009-845b-7efb65de3c5a">
  <data key="d3">If the account value is high enough to absorb monthly charges like the administrative fee, policyholders can forego paying premiums. This financial buffer relies on proper allocation of funds, such as those affected by the 3.5% load.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae" target="0b7e0a06-5166-489d-a873-3b798f915e2c">
  <data key="d3">If the account value is high enough to cover total monthly charges—including COI and administrative fees—the policyholder may skip premium payments without lapsing coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae" target="6bfb8452-bcec-4db6-b212-fd25bdcfbc79">
  <data key="d3">If the account value is insufficient to cover the $12 monthly administrative charge, skipping premium payments would not be sustainable. This charge is part of the financial burden that must be managed within the account balance.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae" target="1b6d4d68-07ed-4c80-987c-ddf958d36f08">
  <data key="d3">If the account value is sufficient to cover total charges, policyholders can skip paying premiums. These charges are consistently deducted on the third day of every month, ensuring predictable financial obligations.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae" target="e2637b0a-dd20-4e01-8fa1-8779d2f346fa">
  <data key="d3">The ability to skip premiums relies on adequate account value, which remains viable due to guaranteed stable COI rates that prevent unexpected increases in fees.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae" target="749f8b25-e9c6-4e2e-a60a-5fdcef1215c4">
  <data key="d3">If the account value is high enough to absorb monthly deductions like COI, policyholders can skip paying premiums. The COI amount itself is calculated using a precise formula involving the death benefit and current account value.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae" target="9639c325-d6a7-4181-a801-0a4fdfaefa94">
  <data key="d3">If the account value is high enough to cover monthly fees, policyholders can skip paying premiums. This same account value level determines the magnitude of the cost-of-insurance deduction, since it's calculated relative to the death benefit shortfall.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="3a04b397-cd4d-461a-8e10-baf1f9c1d92f" target="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">affects account value</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7dc4e868-72f3-4a82-bcc4-2dc4618b20a4" target="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">reduces account value</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a10ab3ab-e6c6-4850-9d07-f3102d640055" target="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">monthly deduction</data>
</edge>
<edge source="331d3e03-d7ec-4dd9-890b-c2d852d57015" target="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">account value</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e6598607-fadd-4c12-905f-0aad288a8f3d" target="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">covered by account value when premiums skipped</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c63da4c9-eaae-4c1f-9ee4-7bd7dd903385" target="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">covered by account value when premiums skipped</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="08297671-4782-4819-a6a9-1473ccbb5f05">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="95ebe390-f4a9-4a87-a597-928d18a03d7d">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="7650a77f-2cf2-4bc7-bad1-dbbd19c55151">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="b78c5928-fb64-4a29-96b6-ae8774ad142a">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">amount</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="48c760de-2670-464d-8364-5750775aa35b">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">amount</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="742e18dd-2ff0-4be4-8a4c-861a509e4cd2">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">amount</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="7c80a6eb-0783-4a8e-b0c9-5e355e97aaf6">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">percentage</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="9d9a7295-ad46-45bc-a6f2-5aa148930295">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">charge</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="18d960e9-4b64-4111-b7e5-f2a041c0d03c">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">charge</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="0226db91-f1c9-4cd1-9aec-54aa60220d1e">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">charge</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="d673b95e-c66c-4b70-b7c6-3888237440a1">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">date</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="99a2ea02-45ff-4204-9c3f-be85350484db">
  <data key="d3">Sufficient account value is necessary to absorb monthly charges, making it possible to rely on floor protection when markets fall without risking lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299">
  <data key="d3">To maintain flexibility in paying premiums, the account value must stay above the threshold needed to cover monthly deductions, which relies on having effective floor protection preventing negative balances.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="116850af-15ce-4679-bcc4-58d5753875d7">
  <data key="d3">Sufficient account value is crucial to withstand monthly deductions; this financial cushion allows the policyholder to skip premium payments safely, especially important given the 5% downside protection feature.</data>
  <data key="d4">necessitated by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="70667dae-ff8c-4bac-bf04-03807ddb6bd7">
  <data key="d3">Sufficient account value to cover monthly deductions relies on preserved principal due to market protections, ensuring long-term sustainability of the policy’s funding.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="a53ff70e-2b10-4259-9e14-fe7adb0931b1">
  <data key="d3">To avoid paying premiums, the account value must remain high enough to absorb monthly deductions; however, earning 0% interest reduces the ability to build such reserves over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">necessitates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="50dee1d7-a696-448d-92e6-11dfe14d068f">
  <data key="d3">Sufficient account value enables the option to skip premium payments, supporting the claim that payments can be made at any time due to built-in financial safeguards.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="86b72d75-5a59-44c2-b2d6-912ce393cf76">
  <data key="d3">To legally or practically skip premium payments, the account value must remain high enough to cover mandatory monthly deductions, which reinforces why payment timing cannot be arbitrary unless supported by adequate reserves.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176">
  <data key="d3">Sufficient account value to cover monthly deductions allows flexibility to skip premium payments; however, such flexibility requires prior contributions meeting the $100 minimum to maintain balance.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa">
  <data key="d3">To legally or contractually skip premium payments, the account value must remain high enough to cover ongoing costs, which implies any such skipped payment still needs to respect the minimum requirement of $100 when made.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2">
  <data key="d3">Maintaining adequate account value to cover monthly fees allows policyholders to potentially skip premium payments, making the $50,000 annual ceiling more meaningful for long-term sustainability.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d">
  <data key="d3">Maintaining enough account value allows for skipped premium payments, making it feasible to meet the long-term goal of sustaining coverage through the recommended $6,000 annual contribution.</data>
  <data key="d4">necessitates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="2bf05a03-d336-46dd-a382-121bb038f1a6">
  <data key="d3">To maintain eligibility for skipping premium payments, the account value must remain high enough to cover recurring costs, which only holds under the assumption that underlying actuarial and financial models remain valid.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae">
  <data key="d3">Sufficient account value is necessary to permit skipping premium payments, ensuring continued policy validity despite non-payment.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d">
  <data key="d3">The need to maintain adequate account value to avoid triggering penalties when skipping payments depends on how much of each premium actually contributes to the account, which is reduced by the 3.5% load.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to maintain sufficient account value hinges on ongoing monthly deductions like the Cost of Insurance, which reduces the balance over time and affects the ability to skip future premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional dependency</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="6c580dbf-ec5e-4009-845b-7efb65de3c5a">
  <data key="d3">A sufficient account value ensures that monthly fees—including those tied to the premium load—are covered, enabling flexibility in premium payments without lapsing coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="6bfb8452-bcec-4db6-b212-fd25bdcfbc79">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that account value covers monthly deductions relies on knowing what those deductions entail; one such deduction is the fixed $12 administrative charge.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="0b7e0a06-5166-489d-a873-3b798f915e2c">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that account value covers monthly deductions relies on knowing exactly what those deductions entail; total monthly charges being composed of COI and admin fees explains why maintaining adequate balance matters.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="749f8b25-e9c6-4e2e-a60a-5fdcef1215c4">
  <data key="d3">If the account value is insufficient due to high COI charges calculated using the given formula, it may prevent the ability to skip premium payments without depleting reserves.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="9639c325-d6a7-4181-a801-0a4fdfaefa94">
  <data key="d3">The requirement to maintain enough account value to skip premium payments depends on the magnitude of the monthly COI deduction, which itself increases with larger gaps between the death benefit and account value.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="1b6d4d68-07ed-4c80-987c-ddf958d36f08">
  <data key="d3">If the account value isn't sufficient to cover total charges, skipping premiums could lead to policy lapse; since these charges are deducted on the third day of each month, ongoing monitoring of the account value relative to this schedule is essential.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="e2637b0a-dd20-4e01-8fa1-8779d2f346fa">
  <data key="d3">The necessity to maintain enough account value to avoid lapses hinges on predictable expenses; since COI rates are capped, they ensure long-term sustainability of the account balance needed to skip payments without triggering termination.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647">
  <data key="d3">Adequate account balance ensures long-term policy viability, making it possible to qualify for policy loans after one year of activity.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5">
  <data key="d3">A sufficiently high account value ensures eligibility for policy loans up to 90% of surrender value, linking financial stability for premium flexibility with access to liquidity.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22">
  <data key="d3">Adequate account value ensures continued coverage despite skipped premiums, which is impacted by outstanding loans that draw from the account. Since loaned amounts still earn 3%, they help preserve some value, reducing risk of lapse.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="6c81117f-d67b-45c8-b7c8-8a2a822df46d">
  <data key="d3">Frequent or large partial withdrawals, especially within the first ten free ones, risk depleting the account value needed to cover ongoing monthly deductions, potentially undermining the ability to skip future premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9">
  <data key="d3">A sufficiently funded account ensures continued coverage despite skipped premiums, which indirectly enables meaningful partial withdrawals like the $500 minimum allowed.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb">
  <data key="d3">Adequate account value ensures premium skips remain viable, and the low net cost of policy loans helps preserve that value over time by minimizing erosion due to borrowing.</data>
  <data key="d4">supprts sustainability</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a">
  <data key="d3">If policyholder loans accumulate, they reduce the account value needed to avoid premium payments, making it harder to meet the threshold required to skip premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e" target="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5">
  <data key="d3">If frequent partial withdrawals occur beyond the allowed number, accumulated fees and reduced account balance may compromise the fund’s ability to support required monthly deductions, risking policy lapse despite intent to skip premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="08297671-4782-4819-a6a9-1473ccbb5f05" target="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">protects against</data>
</edge>
