<edge source="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f" target="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176">
  <data key="d3">Monthly deductions for Cost of Insurance reduce the account value, so consistent premium payments above the $100 minimum help maintain enough funds to absorb such charges without depleting the account prematurely.</data>
  <data key="d4">needs funding from</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f" target="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa">
  <data key="d3">Monthly COI charges reduce the account value, so maintaining a minimum $100 premium helps offset these reductions and preserve long-term coverage sustainability.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f" target="0d35c1ce-d96d-4562-80f8-0654abe126d2">
  <data key="d3">Monthly Cost of Insurance (COI) charges reduce the account value regularly, impacting the sustainability of premium payments up to the $50,000 annual limit. The presence of ongoing COI deductions means contributors must plan carefully to stay within budget despite fixed periodic outflows.</data>
  <data key="d4">modulates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f" target="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d">
  <data key="d3">Monthly deductions such as the Cost of Insurance (COI) contribute to maintaining the policy’s active status, supporting the sustainability implied by the recommended $6,000 annual premium.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f" target="2bf05a03-d336-46dd-a382-121bb038f1a6">
  <data key="d3">Monthly deductions such as the Cost of Insurance contribute to maintaining the policy’s viability over time, supporting the actuarial basis underpinning the $6,000 annual recommendation.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f" target="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae">
  <data key="d3">Monthly deduction of the Cost of Insurance affects the account balance, influencing whether it remains high enough to allow skipping future premium payments without lapsing coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f" target="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e">
  <data key="d3">Since the Cost of Insurance is deducted monthly, it directly influences the account value, making it essential to monitor balances so they remain high enough to permit skipped premium payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">impacts account value</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f" target="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d">
  <data key="d3">Monthly Cost of Insurance charges occur independently but contribute alongside the 3.5% premium load toward reducing the account value over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f" target="749f8b25-e9c6-4e2e-a60a-5fdcef1215c4">
  <data key="d3">The monthly deduction of Cost of Insurance (COI) is governed by a precise calculation based on the death benefit, current account value, and a specified rate. This ensures transparency in how the charge is applied each month.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f" target="0b7e0a06-5166-489d-a873-3b798f915e2c">
  <data key="d3">The deduction of Cost of Insurance (COI) monthly is a specific instance contributing to the overall monthly charges, which also include an administrative fee.</data>
  <data key="d4">part of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f" target="6bfb8452-bcec-4db6-b212-fd25bdcfbc79">
  <data key="d3">The Cost of Insurance (COI) is subtracted monthly from the account value, alongside other recurring charges such as the $12 administrative fee.</data>
  <data key="d4">simultaneously deducted</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f" target="1b6d4d68-07ed-4c80-987c-ddf958d36f08">
  <data key="d3">The Cost of Insurance (COI) is one component of the total monthly charges that are collectively deducted from the account value on the third day of every month.</data>
  <data key="d4">part of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f" target="9639c325-d6a7-4181-a801-0a4fdfaefa94">
  <data key="d3">The monthly deduction of Cost of Insurance (COI) is influenced by the disparity between the death benefit and the current account value, meaning higher differences lead to larger deductions.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f" target="e2637b0a-dd20-4e01-8fa1-8779d2f346fa">
  <data key="d3">The monthly deduction of Cost of Insurance (COI) is made possible due to its guaranteed stability; since COI rates cannot exceed those outlined in the policy schedule, regular deductions remain predictable and secure.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f" target="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e">
  <data key="d3">The monthly deduction of COI contributes to maintaining policy value over time, which influences the calculation of surrender charges when exiting early. Higher accumulated value due to consistent payments may lower effective surrender penalties.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f" target="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332">
  <data key="d3">Monthly COI deductions gradually reduce the account value, which may affect the amount subject to surrender charges if the policy is terminated in Year 4. Higher cumulative COI costs could lower the net cash surrender value.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences value</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f" target="00111295-2bb8-4547-912d-c65ce0d8d633">
  <data key="d3">Monthly COI deductions gradually reduce the account value, affecting the funds available before any surrender charge is applied. In Year 5, a 6% surrender charge may significantly diminish the net amount received upon termination, especially if the account has been eroded by recurring fees.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences value</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f" target="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75">
  <data key="d3">Monthly COI deductions reduce the account value over time, potentially increasing the relative burden of surrender charges later, especially if funds are withdrawn before maturity.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f" target="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00">
  <data key="d3">Monthly COI deductions gradually reduce the account value, affecting the amount available before surrender charges are applied. In Year 9, a 2% surrender charge may further diminish the net cash surrender value derived from that reduced balance.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f" target="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df">
  <data key="d3">The monthly deduction of Cost of Insurance reduces the account value, which affects the basis for calculating surrender charges that are applied to premiums paid in the first decade.</data>
  <data key="d4">indirectly affects</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f" target="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73">
  <data key="d3">Monthly COI deductions reduce the account value over time, affecting the amount available at surrender. By Year 12, when surrender charges vanish, these accumulated reductions may have stabilized the remaining balance, making it more favorable to access funds.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f" target="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a">
  <data key="d3">The monthly deduction of Cost of Insurance reduces the account value, thereby lowering the potential Cash Surrender Value when calculating final payout upon withdrawal or surrender.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f" target="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647">
  <data key="d3">The requirement for consistent monthly COI deductions supports long-term policy sustainability, enabling the policyholder to meet the one-year threshold needed to access policy loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f" target="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5">
  <data key="d3">The monthly deduction of Cost of Insurance reduces the account value, thereby influencing the surrender value used to determine the maximum allowable policy loan.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f" target="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6">
  <data key="d3">Monthly COI deductions reduce the account value, potentially limiting liquidity available for policy loans, though the 4% loan interest rate remains unaffected by these deductions.</data>
  <data key="d4">indirectly affects</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f" target="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a">
  <data key="d3">The monthly deduction of Cost of Insurance reduces the account value, potentially limiting funds available for future loans or impacting overall policy performance, though it does not directly cause death benefit reductions like loans do.</data>
  <data key="d4">indirectly affects</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f" target="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9">
  <data key="d3">The monthly deduction of Cost of Insurance reduces the account value, potentially limiting the funds available for partial withdrawals, which require a minimum of $500. This creates a cumulative effect where sustained COI costs may delay or restrict early liquidity.</data>
  <data key="d4">indirectly affects</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f" target="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22">
  <data key="d3">The monthly deduction of Cost of Insurance reduces the account value, potentially limiting funds available for loans, yet any outstanding loans still accrue interest and earn returns in the fixed account, mitigating part of the cost.</data>
  <data key="d4">partially offsets</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="d045e244-5979-4456-9aa8-fe37bf5a0c5b" target="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">is deducted monthly</data>
</edge>
