<edge source="749f8b25-e9c6-4e2e-a60a-5fdcef1215c4" target="70667dae-ff8c-4bac-bf04-03807ddb6bd7">
  <data key="d3">The cost-of-insurance charge, calculated based on the gap between the death benefit and account value, reflects ongoing costs tied to maintaining coverage, independent of market performance protections.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="749f8b25-e9c6-4e2e-a60a-5fdcef1215c4" target="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa">
  <data key="d3">The monthly COI rate calculation relies on the current account value, which is influenced by regular premium payments—including those at the minimum level of $100—thereby linking the cost mechanism back to basic payment requirements.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="749f8b25-e9c6-4e2e-a60a-5fdcef1215c4" target="a6609e69-c5f5-4d6e-9fa1-fc83061e83ae">
  <data key="d3">The cost-of-insurance charge is derived from the difference between the death benefit and account value, scaled by a rate; this deduction reduces the account balance, thereby influencing whether skipping premiums remains feasible.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="749f8b25-e9c6-4e2e-a60a-5fdcef1215c4" target="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e">
  <data key="d3">The need to maintain adequate account value to avoid triggering premium obligations depends on how much is subtracted via COI, which is determined by the specified formula involving death benefit and account value.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="749f8b25-e9c6-4e2e-a60a-5fdcef1215c4" target="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d">
  <data key="d3">The COI charge is calculated using the account value, which is reduced by the 3.5% premium load. Thus, the load influences the inputs to the COI formula, though it's not part of the formula explicitly.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="749f8b25-e9c6-4e2e-a60a-5fdcef1215c4" target="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f">
  <data key="d3">The formula quantifies the exact amount subtracted monthly for Cost of Insurance, providing operational clarity for why and how the deduction occurs regularly.</data>
  <data key="d4">used in</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="749f8b25-e9c6-4e2e-a60a-5fdcef1215c4" target="9639c325-d6a7-4181-a801-0a4fdfaefa94">
  <data key="d3">The formula for computing the monthly COI uses the difference between the death benefit and the account value as its core component, reflecting how this gap influences the charge amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">used in</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.98</data>
</edge>
<edge source="749f8b25-e9c6-4e2e-a60a-5fdcef1215c4" target="e2637b0a-dd20-4e01-8fa1-8779d2f346fa">
  <data key="d3">The formula for computing the monthly COI relies on a rate that is permanently capped at the level defined in the policy schedule, ensuring predictable calculations over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="749f8b25-e9c6-4e2e-a60a-5fdcef1215c4" target="0b7e0a06-5166-489d-a873-3b798f915e2c">
  <data key="d3">The formula in fact_sentence_1 defines how the Cost of Insurance (COI) charge is calculated, which is a key component included in the total monthly charges mentioned in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="749f8b25-e9c6-4e2e-a60a-5fdcef1215c4" target="1b6d4d68-07ed-4c80-987c-ddf958d36f08">
  <data key="d3">The cost-of-insurance (COI) charge, computed using the given formula, forms part of the total monthly deductions applied to the account value. These combined charges are systematically subtracted on the third day of every month.</data>
  <data key="d4">contributes to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
