<edge source="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199" target="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906">
  <data key="d3">Option 1's designation as offering a level death benefit means the payout remains unchanged throughout the policy term, specifically set at $500,000.</data>
  <data key="d4">defined by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199" target="1ff5fee4-2e90-43f5-9b90-379cb6250678">
  <data key="d3">Option 1 offers a fixed death benefit regardless of account performance, contrasting with Option 2, which increases the payout based on accumulated account value alongside the base specification.</data>
  <data key="d4">contrasts</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199" target="f48d18db-916a-4e9a-ad5c-8b176c59da3c">
  <data key="d3">The level death benefit feature defines the payout structure of Option 1, whereas its lower ongoing charges reflect reduced expenses over time. Together, they highlight key financial characteristics of the plan.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199" target="9dd93a2e-b1e4-427c-b771-0da3121d9f76">
  <data key="d3">Option 1 defines a stable death benefit amount, providing a baseline feature that enables the possibility of switching to other options like the increasing type.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199" target="3d7d5200-92e7-4186-968d-e19ab1fbc8b6">
  <data key="d3">Option 1 offers a constant death benefit amount, providing predictability, whereas Option 2 allows the death benefit to grow dynamically based on account performance, offering higher long-term potential but less stability.</data>
  <data key="d4">contrasts</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199" target="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25">
  <data key="d3">The presence of a Level death benefit option enables policyholders to consider switching plans, making the requirement for advance notice applicable when modifying such benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199" target="554b41df-0ff4-46de-a895-a7a081334009">
  <data key="d3">Under Option 1's level death benefit framework, the maximum partial withdrawal is limited by the account value less any applicable surrender charge, ensuring that withdrawals do not exceed what remains after penalties.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199" target="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb">
  <data key="d3">Under Option 1’s level death benefit structure, any outstanding policy loans reduce the final payout. The net annual cost of such loans being 1% reflects an ongoing expense tied to accessing cash value, thereby indirectly impacting the stability of the promised death benefit over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199" target="024598e4-2394-4fad-b636-543f3ffb9225">
  <data key="d3">The Level Death Benefit in Option 1 creates a stable foundation where any partial withdrawal results in an equivalent decrease in the payout amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199" target="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a">
  <data key="d3">The level death benefit in Option 1 serves as the baseline payout, but it is reduced by any outstanding policy loans when a claim is made.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199" target="db5f42b7-e216-4454-b4f0-97dfc9c2dbc6">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 states that Option 1 provides a level death benefit, which directly supports and clarifies the specific feature referenced in fact_sentence_1 about the selected benefit option.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199" target="deefe5c8-640f-408f-a9d3-69fdb6670c3a">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 identifies Option 1 as offering a level death benefit, which explains why the initial face amount stated in fact_sentence_1 remains constant over time without adjustment.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.98</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199" target="03f1141d-d1b6-49f8-a326-19f21e643d95">
  <data key="d3">The statement about Option 1 providing a level death benefit explains why the $6,000 annual premium is applicable, as this premium supports the fixed-benefit structure rather than variable or growing benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="73bd2f26-cebc-4371-9343-b0fc4d54d2e7" target="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">has option</data>
</edge>
