</edge>
<edge source="f48d18db-916a-4e9a-ad5c-8b176c59da3c" target="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906">
  <data key="d3">Lower ongoing charges make Option 1 financially advantageous, especially given its guaranteed $500,000 death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">enhances value of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f48d18db-916a-4e9a-ad5c-8b176c59da3c" target="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199">
  <data key="d3">Lower ongoing charges contribute to better long-term value retention, complementing the stability offered by Option 1's level death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f48d18db-916a-4e9a-ad5c-8b176c59da3c" target="99ca8905-b57d-4689-9164-12678eda198b">
  <data key="d3">Option 1's lower ongoing charges contrast with Option 2’s higher charges, highlighting a key financial distinction between the two death benefit choices.</data>
  <data key="d4">comparative difference</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f48d18db-916a-4e9a-ad5c-8b176c59da3c" target="3d7d5200-92e7-4186-968d-e19ab1fbc8b6">
  <data key="d3">Option 1 offers reduced ongoing expenses, making it more cost-efficient than other plans like Option 2, which prioritizes growing benefits despite potentially higher fees.</data>
  <data key="d4">comparative feature</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f48d18db-916a-4e9a-ad5c-8b176c59da3c" target="554b41df-0ff4-46de-a895-a7a081334009">
  <data key="d3">Lower ongoing charges in Option 1 affect long-term cost efficiency, influencing how much liquidity remains accessible via withdrawals. This impacts the effective maximum partial withdrawal amount, especially when combined with surrender charges.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.68</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f48d18db-916a-4e9a-ad5c-8b176c59da3c" target="024598e4-2394-4fad-b636-543f3ffb9225">
  <data key="d3">Option 1's lower ongoing charges make it financially efficient, while its partial withdrawals directly reduce the death benefit proportionally. This reflects a structural trade-off where cost savings coexist with immediate benefit erosion upon withdrawals.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a77308b7-5f15-4b31-a8ce-e54c20412b82" target="f48d18db-916a-4e9a-ad5c-8b176c59da3c">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">is positively affected by</data>
</edge>
