<edge source="9dd93a2e-b1e4-427c-b771-0da3121d9f76" target="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906">
  <data key="d3">The availability of switching between death benefit options allows a policyholder to move away from the fixed $500,000 level benefit offered by Option 1.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dd93a2e-b1e4-427c-b771-0da3121d9f76" target="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199">
  <data key="d3">The ability to switch death benefit options annually relies on having defined alternatives, such as the Level option described in Sentence 1.</data>
  <data key="d4">required for</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dd93a2e-b1e4-427c-b771-0da3121d9f76" target="1ff5fee4-2e90-43f5-9b90-379cb6250678">
  <data key="d3">The right to switch between death benefit options relies on knowing how each option calculates its payout, including that Option 2 includes an account value component.</data>
  <data key="d4">informs</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dd93a2e-b1e4-427c-b771-0da3121d9f76" target="3d7d5200-92e7-4186-968d-e19ab1fbc8b6">
  <data key="d3">The ability to switch death benefit options annually allows policyholders to adapt their coverage strategy. This includes transitioning into Option 2, where benefits grow with account value.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dd93a2e-b1e4-427c-b771-0da3121d9f76" target="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25">
  <data key="d3">Switching death benefit options requires an annual decision on the policy anniversary, but it cannot occur without providing at least 60 days’ prior notification to ensure administrative processing.</data>
  <data key="d4">requires notice</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dd93a2e-b1e4-427c-b771-0da3121d9f76" target="3493040d-88ba-470b-9604-c6e5ce8f6501">
  <data key="d3">Switching to an increased death benefit requires proof of insurability, meaning that while switches are allowed annually, not all transitions are unconditional—they depend on health qualification when raising coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dd93a2e-b1e4-427c-b771-0da3121d9f76" target="e9cf97a9-cf24-4d3c-adf8-586c6935d0e1">
  <data key="d3">The ability to switch death benefit options applies within the framework established by Horizon Wealth Protection Insurance, whose authority governs such policy provisions.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
