</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="1ff5fee4-2e90-43f5-9b90-379cb6250678">
  <data key="d3">The maximum loan allowed depends on the surrender value, which itself influences the total death benefit under Option 2 when combined with the specified amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="6f98a9e1-688e-4680-b305-6c7ecf379647">
  <data key="d3">Once the policy has been active for one year, borrowers may access up to 90% of the surrender value as a loan.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6">
  <data key="d3">The maximum loan amount is capped at 90% of the surrender value, and this borrowed sum accrues interest at a fixed annual rate of 4%, determining the total repayment obligation.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22">
  <data key="d3">The maximum loan amount is capped at 90% of the surrender value, ensuring that any funds withdrawn remain within defined limits. These borrowed funds continue to earn interest at the fixed account rate of 3%, contributing to overall policy performance.</data>
  <data key="d4">limits</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb">
  <data key="d3">The maximum loan limit of 90% of surrender value sets the basis for calculating the actual cost of borrowing. This constraint determines the scale of the loan, which directly influences the net annual cost derived from the interest differential.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="554b41df-0ff4-46de-a895-a7a081334009">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 establishes that loans cannot exceed 90% of surrender value, limiting access to cash. Fact sentence 2 specifies that partial withdrawals are capped by the remaining account value after deducting any applicable surrender charges, reflecting another constraint on fund availability.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a">
  <data key="d3">The maximum allowable loan is set at 90% of the surrender value, enabling borrowers to access significant funds. However, any unpaid loans reduce the final death benefit paid out when the policyholder passes away.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e">
  <data key="d3">The maximum loan amount depends on the surrender value, which itself is reduced by surrender charges applied in the first 12 years, meaning these two facts jointly constrain borrowing capacity during early policy tenure.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018">
  <data key="d3">The maximum loan amount depends on the surrender value, which is reduced by the 10% Year 1 surrender charge, limiting the effective collateral available for loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890">
  <data key="d3">The maximum loan amount depends on the surrender value, which is reduced by the surrender charge in Year 2. Therefore, the 9% surrender charge limits the usable portion of the account value for borrowing purposes.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332">
  <data key="d3">The maximum loan amount depends on the surrender value, which is reduced by the 7% surrender charge in Year 4, thus constraining the effective loanable amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b">
  <data key="d3">The maximum loan amount depends on the surrender value, which is reduced by the surrender charge applicable in Year 3. Therefore, knowing the 8% charge helps determine the true usable surrender value for loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="00111295-2bb8-4547-912d-c65ce0d8d633">
  <data key="d3">The maximum loan amount depends on the surrender value, which is reduced by the surrender charge in Year 5. Thus, knowing the 6% charge helps determine the effective surrender value eligible for borrowing.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="84b84dec-45b7-4ca8-ae2f-a68466866f24">
  <data key="d3">The maximum loan amount depends on the surrender value, which is reduced by the surrender charge in Year 6. Thus, knowing the 5% charge helps determine the true usable surrender value for borrowing purposes.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="29e19c25-f1c1-4c3e-8db6-46bce82c0dca">
  <data key="d3">The maximum loan amount depends on the surrender value, which is reduced by the surrender charge in Year 7. Thus, knowing the 4% surrender charge helps determine the true usable portion of the surrender value for borrowing purposes.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75">
  <data key="d3">The maximum loan amount depends on the surrender value, which itself is reduced by surrender charges like the 3% assessed in Year 8. This means the actual usable surrender value—and thus the loan ceiling—is affected by ongoing charges.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00">
  <data key="d3">The maximum loan amount depends on the surrender value, which itself is reduced by surrender charges like the 2% charge in Year 9. Thus, higher future surrender charges could indirectly constrain effective loan availability.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86">
  <data key="d3">The maximum loan amount depends on the surrender value, which is reduced by surrender charges like the 0.5% in Year 11. Thus, lower surrender charges increase usable surrender value and indirectly support higher allowable loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="a3cf559b-392a-434d-8391-67212bc086c3">
  <data key="d3">The maximum loan amount relies on the surrender value, which is diminished by surrender charges like the 1% charge in Year 10. Thus, knowing the surrender charge helps determine the true usable portion of the surrender value for borrowing.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73">
  <data key="d3">The availability of policy loans up to 90% of surrender value becomes fully advantageous after Year 12, when surrender charges drop to zero, allowing risk-free borrowing against accumulated value.</data>
  <data key="d4">enhances</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df">
  <data key="d3">The maximum loan amount depends on the surrender value, which itself is affected by surrender charges tied to premiums paid early in the policy term.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a">
  <data key="d3">The maximum loan amount depends on the surrender value, which itself is derived by deducting surrender charges and outstanding loans from the account value, making the computation of surrender value essential to determining allowable loan limits.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b">
  <data key="d3">The maximum loan amount being tied to surrender value complements the availability of free partial withdrawals after Year 1, as both provide liquidity options without immediate penalties, enhancing policyholder access to funds.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="9d636a77-9852-432c-b8fb-7593d751a2da">
  <data key="d3">The maximum loan amount is constrained by surrender value, while partial withdrawals are limited to 10% of account value annually. These mechanisms allow fund access via distinct pathways—one borrowing against value, the other drawing from accumulated value—without direct overlap.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f">
  <data key="d3">A higher surrender value due to lower COI impact allows greater policy loan capacity, making the loan limit dependent on the ongoing effect of COI deductions.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="6bfb8452-bcec-4db6-b212-fd25bdcfbc79">
  <data key="d3">The policy’s maximum loan limit of 90% of surrender value depends on accumulated account value, which is affected by periodic charges such as the $12 monthly administrative fee mentioned earlier.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e">
  <data key="d3">The ability to skip premium payments hinges on having enough account value, which directly affects the maximum loanable amount based on surrender value.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5" target="70667dae-ff8c-4bac-bf04-03807ddb6bd7">
  <data key="d3">Policy loans up to 90% of surrender value depend on sustained account value, which is protected from market losses per the principle stated in fact_sentence_1, ensuring reliable collateral availability.</data>
  <data key="d4">enhances</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
