  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">fees</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9" target="a81b7eea-6ab0-4414-a9d4-364b94787bb7">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9" target="cfe5e7a9-a1dd-402b-bf8e-50c2fc3fb269">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">charge</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9" target="73f70bf3-ce7b-4dba-ad51-89660a188442">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">year</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9" target="6a5f0039-dbcb-48db-8f7a-e00d6a258f28">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">year</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9" target="554b41df-0ff4-46de-a895-a7a081334009">
  <data key="d3">The minimum withdrawal is set at $500, ensuring small but meaningful access to funds. The maximum allowable withdrawal depends on the current account value adjusted for any applicable surrender charge, capping how much can be withdrawn without triggering penalties.</data>
  <data key="d4">constrains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9" target="6c81117f-d67b-45c8-b7c8-8a2a822df46d">
  <data key="d3">The requirement of a $500 minimum withdrawal enables access to fee-free partial withdrawals, making it possible for policyholders to withdraw funds without penalty when meeting the threshold.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9" target="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5">
  <data key="d3">The requirement of a $500 minimum ensures withdrawals occur meaningfully, enabling the application of subsequent rules like the $50 fee after the tenth withdrawal.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9" target="024598e4-2394-4fad-b636-543f3ffb9225">
  <data key="d3">The requirement that partial withdrawals must be at least $500 sets the baseline for when the reduction mechanism applies. This ensures only meaningful withdrawals trigger changes to the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditions</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9" target="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f">
  <data key="d3">A minimum partial withdrawal of $500 affects how policyholders manage their account balances, influencing whether sufficient funds remain after COI deductions to support future withdrawals without depleting reserves.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences account value</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9" target="45f97aed-091e-480b-b637-f618f4e2486e">
  <data key="d3">The $500 minimum withdrawal requirement depends on having adequate account value to avoid violating conditions needed to skip premium payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9" target="7d57accf-750c-4143-addd-8dbbeb124299">
  <data key="d3">Setting the minimum partial withdrawal at $500 implies users need sufficient account balance to meet this threshold, which becomes increasingly challenging given the lack of floor protection—any decline below zero would eliminate buffer capacity entirely.</data>
  <data key="d4">exposes vulnerability</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.68</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9" target="70667dae-ff8c-4bac-bf04-03807ddb6bd7">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a $500 minimum partial withdrawal threshold implies that policyholders have accessible liquidity only when sufficient funds remain, which is made possible because market losses do not affect principal—a key feature enabling predictable withdrawal availability over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9" target="e9cf97a9-cf24-4d3c-adf8-586c6935d0e1">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 outlines a key feature of the policy's withdrawal mechanism, relevant to users of Horizon Wealth Protection Insurance’s products. This detail is consistent with the type of financial product described in the broader document issued by the organization.</data>
  <data key="d4">contextual support</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9" target="79f032d3-1299-41de-85c7-f944c1411556">
  <data key="d3">The $500 minimum partial withdrawal requirement is governed by policies established in this document, whose authority and timing are confirmed by its execution date of October 3, 2024.</data>
  <data key="d4">contextualizes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
