<edge source="024598e4-2394-4fad-b636-543f3ffb9225" target="ec56b365-0020-450d-9cc6-283a79189906">
  <data key="d3">Since partial withdrawals under Option 1 reduce the death benefit dollar-for-dollar, the original $500,000 base is diminished each time funds are taken out, making the initial figure essential for understanding the reduction mechanism.</data>
  <data key="d4">caused by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="024598e4-2394-4fad-b636-543f3ffb9225" target="e1d7d59c-ecc5-48bc-b7c4-1fd4fcfbe199">
  <data key="d3">Because Option 1 features a Level Death Benefit, each partial withdrawal reduces the final death benefit by its full monetary value.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="024598e4-2394-4fad-b636-543f3ffb9225" target="f48d18db-916a-4e9a-ad5c-8b176c59da3c">
  <data key="d3">The death benefit under Option 1 decreases dollar-for-dollar with partial withdrawals, reinforcing why maintaining lower ongoing charges helps preserve policy value over time despite such deductions.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="024598e4-2394-4fad-b636-543f3ffb9225" target="f75970d5-49e2-416e-98bf-26056a65e3f9">
  <data key="d3">Any partial withdrawal made under Option 1 results in an equivalent reduction in the death benefit, but only if it meets or exceeds the $500 minimum threshold established earlier.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="024598e4-2394-4fad-b636-543f3ffb9225" target="554b41df-0ff4-46de-a895-a7a081334009">
  <data key="d3">Under Option 1, each partial withdrawal reduces the death benefit dollar-for-dollar. Since the size of such withdrawals cannot exceed the account value minus the surrender charge, the reduction in death benefit is bounded accordingly.</data>
  <data key="d4">directly reduces</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="024598e4-2394-4fad-b636-543f3ffb9225" target="6c81117f-d67b-45c8-b7c8-8a2a822df46d">
  <data key="d3">Each partial withdrawal under Option 1 directly lowers the death benefit, regardless of whether it incurs a fee or not, meaning even free withdrawals impact the final payout.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="024598e4-2394-4fad-b636-543f3ffb9225" target="7aff69d9-e95c-4762-9fc3-9b84d35f05e5">
  <data key="d3">Under Option 1, every partial withdrawal decreases the death benefit equally. Subsequent withdrawals past the tenth trigger an additional $50 fee.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="024598e4-2394-4fad-b636-543f3ffb9225" target="e56d9b1f-113b-4961-abbd-159d8047aeca">
  <data key="d3">While the Global Diversified Index Account offers a 100% participation rate ensuring maximum creditable gains, any partial withdrawals under Option 1 reduce the death benefit proportionally, thereby diminishing the overall financial outcome despite strong indexing performance.</data>
  <data key="d4">moderated by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="024598e4-2394-4fad-b636-543f3ffb9225" target="af34274c-dfee-4fb4-a491-3e2e93de0364">
  <data key="d3">The rule that partial withdrawals reduce the death benefit under Option 1 interacts with the guaranteed minimum fixed account rates by influencing how much money remains in the policy over time. Stable, low-risk returns help preserve capital, potentially reducing the need for large withdrawals and preserving more of the death benefit.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="f9d34bee-daea-4ed5-ab9d-325e08298c76" target="024598e4-2394-4fad-b636-543f3ffb9225">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">is reduced by</data>
</edge>
<edge source="27cdf665-a74b-4f2d-9759-d1e7782203c8" target="024598e4-2394-4fad-b636-543f3ffb9225">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">is reduced by</data>
</edge>
