<edge source="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018" target="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e">
  <data key="d3">The 10% surrender charge in Year 1 illustrates how surrender fees operate under the broader rule that such charges exist for the first 12 years.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018" target="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890">
  <data key="d3">Year 1 has a surrender charge of 10%, which sets the baseline for the declining schedule. In Year 2, the charge reduces to 9%, consistent with the stated annual decrease.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.98</data>
</edge>
<edge source="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018" target="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b">
  <data key="d3">Year 1 has a surrender charge of 10%, which declines annually. By Year 3, the charge reduces to 8%, reflecting the ongoing downward trend established in the first year.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018" target="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332">
  <data key="d3">Year 1 has the highest surrender charge at 10%, which declines progressively. By Year 4, the charge reduces to 7%, reflecting the stated annual decline schedule.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018" target="00111295-2bb8-4547-912d-c65ce0d8d633">
  <data key="d3">Year 1 has the highest surrender charge at 10%, which declines progressively. By Year 5, the charge reduces to 6%, reflecting the scheduled annual drop outlined in the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018" target="29e19c25-f1c1-4c3e-8db6-46bce82c0dca">
  <data key="d3">Year 1 has the highest surrender charge at 10%, which decreases progressively. By Year 7, it reduces to 4%, reflecting an annual decline in charges over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018" target="84b84dec-45b7-4ca8-ae2f-a68466866f24">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge starts at 10% in Year 1 and decreases each subsequent year, so by Year 6 it reduces to 5%, reflecting the scheduled decline outlined in the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018" target="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge starts at 10% in Year 1 and decreases each subsequent year. By Year 8, it has reduced to 3%, reflecting an ongoing downward trend.</data>
  <data key="d4">decreases to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018" target="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge starts at 10% in Year 1 and decreases each subsequent year, so by Year 9 it has reduced to 2%, reflecting the scheduled annual drop outlined in the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">decreases to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018" target="a3cf559b-392a-434d-8391-67212bc086c3">
  <data key="d3">Year 1 has the highest surrender charge at 10%, which gradually reduces each subsequent year, reaching 1% by Year 10 due to an established annual decrement schedule.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018" target="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86">
  <data key="d3">Year 1 features the highest surrender charge at 10%, setting the baseline for an annual decline. By Year 11, the charge has reduced significantly to 0.5%, reflecting the ongoing decrease outlined in the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">decreased to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018" target="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df">
  <data key="d3">The 10% surrender charge in Year 1 is directly determined by the method stated in fact_sentence_2, where charges are based on premiums paid within the first ten years.</data>
  <data key="d4">derives from</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018" target="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge starts at 10% in Year 1 and decreases each subsequent year until it reaches 0% in Year 12 or beyond, reflecting a time-based reduction in penalty.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018" target="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a">
  <data key="d3">The 10% surrender charge in Year 1 is a key component used in computing the cash surrender value by being subtracted from the account value along with any outstanding loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018" target="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b">
  <data key="d3">The 10% surrender charge in Year 1 sets a condition under which early withdrawals would incur penalties. After Year 1, this penalty ceases to apply, allowing tax-free partial withdrawals without additional fees.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018" target="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a">
  <data key="d3">A 10% surrender charge in Year 1 means that withdrawing funds early incurs significant penalties, increasing the likelihood of losing the entire surrender value if the policy lapses due to non-payment or other reasons.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018" target="e6aa2762-a82e-4371-9d8e-da19a25dd6d1">
  <data key="d3">High surrender charges in Year 1 could discourage early withdrawal from the S&amp;P 500 Index Account, potentially affecting utilization of its annual point-to-point gains.</data>
  <data key="d4">moderated by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018" target="a0671d34-e31b-4b17-8ed5-6a9d495c5148">
  <data key="d3">A 10% surrender charge in Year 1 may discourage early termination despite the potential for annual gains under the S&amp;P 500 Index Account’s one-year crediting period, creating a disincentive to withdraw before full benefit accrual.</data>
  <data key="d4">moderated by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018" target="22fdc352-4139-456b-bd73-2207bfdefc4e">
  <data key="d3">A 10% surrender charge in Year 1 reduces the net amount received upon withdrawal, which may diminish the effective return even when the 100% participation rate leads to strong index-linked growth.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018" target="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176">
  <data key="d3">A 10% surrender charge in Year 1 depends on prior premium payments, reinforcing the importance of meeting the $100 minimum to avoid invalidating future penalty calculations based on actual contributions.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018" target="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa">
  <data key="d3">High surrender charges in Year 1 incentivize consistent premium payments at or above the minimum level to avoid substantial losses upon early cancellation, making adherence to the $100 minimum more financially prudent.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018" target="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2">
  <data key="d3">The 10% surrender charge in Year 1 depends on the total premiums paid, so knowing the $50,000 annual limit helps determine the maximum possible charge under this provision.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018" target="0d35c1ce-d96d-4562-80f8-0654abe126d2">
  <data key="d3">The 10% surrender charge in Year 1 affects any funds withdrawn before maturity, particularly those derived from annual payments capped at $50,000, linking it to the tax-qualified contribution limits.</data>
  <data key="d4">bound by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018" target="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d">
  <data key="d3">A 10% surrender charge in Year 1 underscores the importance of consistent premium payments like the recommended $6,000, since failing to meet them could trigger a lapse before benefits fully accrue.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018" target="6bfb8452-bcec-4db6-b212-fd25bdcfbc79">
  <data key="d3">A high surrender charge in Year 1 reduces the amount available upon withdrawal, potentially diminishing the effective return on payments made, including those covering the $12 monthly administrative fee.</data>
  <data key="d4">financial impact</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018" target="0b7e0a06-5166-489d-a873-3b798f915e2c">
  <data key="d3">The 10% surrender charge in Year 1 reduces the net proceeds from any withdrawal, making it more costly to access funds that have already been diminished by recurring monthly charges like COI and administration fees.</data>
  <data key="d4">increases cost of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018" target="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 identifies a significant financial consequence (10% surrender charge) in Year 1, which could influence whether a policyholder chooses to exercise the option to change death benefits under the 60-day window described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences decision</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018" target="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5">
  <data key="d3">The 10% surrender charge in Year 1 reduces the surrender value, thereby lowering the upper bound of the 90% loan limit derived from that value.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences limit</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018" target="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6">
  <data key="d3">The 10% surrender charge in Year 1 impacts decisions about policy cancellation, indirectly affecting the attractiveness of taking a loan at 4%, as high surrender fees may discourage liquidation even if low-cost loans are available.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018" target="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22">
  <data key="d3">The 10% surrender charge in Year 1 reflects a significant early exit cost, which interacts with the loan mechanism described in fact_sentence_1 where borrowing leads to a net 1% annual cost, compounding total financial impact when combining withdrawal and loan strategies.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018" target="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a">
  <data key="d3">The 10% surrender charge in Year 1 reflects an early penalty that, combined with existing loans, reduces the net amount available to beneficiaries, amplifying the reduction caused by outstanding loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">compounds with</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="4d8b34a6-b85e-4a01-84dc-792a3a136f4d" target="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">has surrender charge</data>
