<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e">
  <data key="d3">The 9% surrender charge in Year 2 exemplifies the broader rule that charges decline annually over the first 12 years, starting from 10%.</data>
  <data key="d4">part of sequence</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge drops from 10% in Year 1 to 9% in Year 2, reflecting the scheduled annual reduction outlined in the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">follows</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.98</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b">
  <data key="d3">Year 2's surrender charge of 9% logically precedes and sets the stage for Year 3’s reduced rate of 8%, reflecting an ongoing annual reduction schedule.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="00111295-2bb8-4547-912d-c65ce0d8d633">
  <data key="d3">Year 2's surrender charge of 9% occurs before Year 5’s 6%, reflecting the gradual annual decrease described in the chunk summary. This progression shows how surrender charges diminish predictably over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332">
  <data key="d3">Year 2 has a surrender charge of 9%, which is higher than the 7% charge in Year 4, reflecting the gradual reduction in fees over time as stated in the chunk summary.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75">
  <data key="d3">Year 2 has a higher surrender charge than Year 8, reflecting the declining nature of charges over time as stated in the chunk summary.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes and decreases</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="84b84dec-45b7-4ca8-ae2f-a68466866f24">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states the surrender charge in Year 2 is 9%, setting an early point in the declining schedule. Fact sentence 2 continues this trend by specifying that by Year 6, the charge has decreased further to 5%, illustrating the annual reduction over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="29e19c25-f1c1-4c3e-8db6-46bce82c0dca">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states the surrender charge in Year 2 is 9%, which aligns with the initial high rate that decreases each subsequent year. Fact sentence 2 shows the charge has reduced to 4% by Year 7, reflecting the ongoing downward trend established in the earlier year.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes and decreases</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86">
  <data key="d3">Year 2's surrender charge of 9% sets an early point in the declining sequence that continues through subsequent years, culminating in a minimal 0.5% charge by Year 11.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="a3cf559b-392a-434d-8391-67212bc086c3">
  <data key="d3">Year 2 has a surrender charge of 9%, reflecting an early stage in the declining schedule. By Year 10, the charge reduces further to 1%, demonstrating the ongoing downward trend established earlier.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00">
  <data key="d3">Year 2 has a surrender charge of 9%, reflecting the initial phase of the declining schedule. By Year 9, the charge has decreased further to 2%, illustrating the ongoing reduction trend within the 12-year window.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 2 being 9% aligns with the rule that charges decline annually based on premiums paid within the first ten years. This reflects the mechanism by which the charge is determined.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 2 is set at 9%, which is applied when calculating the cash surrender value. This specific rate serves as an input into the formula that determines the final cash surrender value.</data>
  <data key="d4">contributes to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73">
  <data key="d3">Year 2 has a surrender charge of 9%, reflecting an ongoing reduction from the initial 10% rate. By Year 12, the cumulative decrease brings the charge down to 0%, completing the scheduled phase-out.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge being 9% in Year 2 reflects the declining schedule within the first decade, while the ability to take free partial withdrawals after Year 1 ensures policyholders can access funds without triggering these charges.</data>
  <data key="d4">consistent with</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.87</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 2 is set at 9%, reflecting the declining schedule. After a policy lapses due to non-payment, any residual surrender value is lost entirely.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="eec22563-c8f9-4930-abc2-6252103b7b77">
  <data key="d3">A 9% surrender charge in Year 2 reflects a cost associated with exiting the policy early, which may influence decisions about whether to rely on the Floor Rate's protection over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="e6aa2762-a82e-4371-9d8e-da19a25dd6d1">
  <data key="d3">A 9% surrender charge in Year 2 could reduce the net benefit realized from gains earned through the S&amp;P 500 Index Account, especially if funds are withdrawn prematurely.</data>
  <data key="d4">impacted by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="a0671d34-e31b-4b17-8ed5-6a9d495c5148">
  <data key="d3">A 9% surrender charge in Year 2 impacts the effective return realized from the S&amp;P 500 Index Account’s annual crediting mechanism, reducing the net benefit when withdrawing before full maturity despite positive index gains.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="b0213eb9-bcd3-41f0-9381-ae8e81ac0f24">
  <data key="d3">A 9% surrender charge in Year 2 affects the effective benefit of returns credited under the NASDAQ-100 Index Account’s one-year crediting period, potentially reducing overall profitability if the policyholder withdraws funds prematurely.</data>
  <data key="d4">financial impact</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176">
  <data key="d3">A 9% surrender charge in Year 2 depends on prior premium payments, reinforcing the importance of meeting the $100 minimum threshold to generate meaningful account value subject to such fees.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa">
  <data key="d3">A high surrender charge in Year 2 (9%) incentivizes continued premium payments at or above the minimum level ($100) to avoid significant losses upon early cancellation, reinforcing the importance of meeting basic payment thresholds.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2">
  <data key="d3">The 9% surrender charge in Year 2 depends on accumulated premiums, so the $50,000 annual premium limit determines the upper bound of what could trigger such a charge.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="0d35c1ce-d96d-4562-80f8-0654abe126d2">
  <data key="d3">A 9% surrender charge in Year 2 reflects one component of early policy termination costs, which may impact whether high contributions near the $50,000 annual cap are financially viable long-term.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d">
  <data key="d3">A 9% surrender charge in Year 2 underscores the need to adhere to the recommended $6,000 annual premium to prevent costly penalties on premature policy termination.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d">
  <data key="d3">The 9% surrender charge in Year 2 depends on accumulated funds, which are reduced by the 3.5% premium load per payment, meaning the load diminishes the base upon which the surrender penalty is computed.</data>
  <data key="d4">reduces base value</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="6bfb8452-bcec-4db6-b212-fd25bdcfbc79">
  <data key="d3">A 9% surrender charge in Year 2 reflects the financial penalty for exiting the policy early, making it more costly to terminate compared to later years. This contrasts with the steady $12 monthly administrative fee, which persists regardless of surrender timing.</data>
  <data key="d4">financial penalty context</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="0b7e0a06-5166-489d-a873-3b798f915e2c">
  <data key="d3">A 9% surrender charge in Year 2 reflects a significant deduction from the account value upon cancellation, potentially offsetting gains made despite low monthly charges. Since monthly charges already reduce the account balance incrementally, the combined effect could diminish liquidity and discourage early surrender.</data>
  <data key="d4">amplifies cost</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.78</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 identifies a 9% surrender charge in Year 2, consistent with the declining schedule mentioned in chunk_summary_2. This detail supports the understanding of financial implications tied to timing, indirectly reinforcing why advance planning—including 60-day notice—is important when altering benefits before such charges take effect.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5">
  <data key="d3">The 9% surrender charge in Year 2 reduces the surrender value, thereby lowering the upper bound of the 90% loan limit derived from that value.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences limit</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6">
  <data key="d3">The Year 2 surrender charge of 9% contextualizes the financial implications of exiting the policy early, reinforcing why the 4% loan interest rate might represent an attractive alternative to surrendering before full accumulation.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb">
  <data key="d3">The Year 2 surrender charge impacts the cash surrender value, potentially influencing whether a policyholder opts for a loan instead of surrendering. However, the 1% net loan cost remains unaffected by surrender charges unless the policy is terminated.</data>
  <data key="d4">independently relevant</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 highlights how loans affect death benefits, while fact_sentence_2 adds specificity to the surrender charge schedule, indirectly reinforcing the overall financial framework affecting policy value and claims outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d4">supplements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890" target="79f032d3-1299-41de-85c7-f944c1411556">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge rate described applies to policies under discussion at the time of this document's issuance on October 3, 2024, placing it within a relevant timeframe for enforcement or reference.</data>
  <data key="d4">timing context</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
