<edge source="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b" target="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e">
  <data key="d3">Sentence 2 identifies the surrender charge in Year 3 as 8%, which exemplifies the broader condition stated in Sentence 1—surrender charges applying within the first 12 years. It serves as an illustrative case under the general rule.</data>
  <data key="d4">is example of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b" target="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge starts at 10% in Year 1 and gradually drops, reaching 8% by Year 3, consistent with the stated annual decline over the first 12 years.</data>
  <data key="d4">follows</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b" target="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890">
  <data key="d3">Year 3’s surrender charge of 8% follows directly from Year 2’s 9%, demonstrating a sequential decrease aligned with the stated annual drop in charges.</data>
  <data key="d4">follows</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b" target="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332">
  <data key="d3">Year 4's lower surrender charge of 7% continues the annual decline initiated in Year 3’s 8% rate, reflecting the scheduled reduction schedule outlined in the chunk summary.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b" target="84b84dec-45b7-4ca8-ae2f-a68466866f24">
  <data key="d3">Year 3 has a surrender charge of 8%, and by Year 6, it has decreased further to 5%, reflecting the annual decline described in the chunk summary.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b" target="00111295-2bb8-4547-912d-c65ce0d8d633">
  <data key="d3">Year 3's surrender charge of 8% precedes and sets the context for Year 5’s reduced rate of 6%, reflecting the ongoing annual decline in charges throughout the initial 12-year period.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b" target="29e19c25-f1c1-4c3e-8db6-46bce82c0dca">
  <data key="d3">Year 3 has a surrender charge of 8%, reflecting an earlier stage in the declining schedule that continues into later years like Year 7.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b" target="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75">
  <data key="d3">Year 3 has a higher surrender charge (8%) than Year 8 (3%), reflecting the declining nature of charges over time as stated in the chunk summary.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes and decreases</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b" target="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00">
  <data key="d3">Year 3's surrender charge of 8% fits into a progressive reduction pattern that continues through subsequent years, leading to lower charges such as the 2% observed in Year 9.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b" target="a3cf559b-392a-434d-8391-67212bc086c3">
  <data key="d3">Year 3's surrender charge of 8% fits into the overall downward trend where charges reduce each year until they reach 0 by Year 12. This context helps explain why Year 10’s charge is only 1%.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b" target="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 3 being 8% is determined by applying the annual percentage formula based on premiums paid within the initial ten-year window.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b" target="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86">
  <data key="d3">Year 3's surrender charge of 8% fits into the gradual reduction trend that continues toward zero by Year 12, making it part of an ongoing sequence where charges diminish each year.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b" target="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 3 (8%) is used as a component in calculating the cash surrender value by being subtracted from the account value along with any outstanding loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">used in calculation</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b" target="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73">
  <data key="d3">Year 3 has an 8% surrender charge, consistent with the declining schedule beginning at 10%, showing progress toward the final reduction. By Year 12, the cumulative effect of annual decreases reaches 0%, completing the phase-out.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b" target="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a">
  <data key="d3">A surrender charge of 8% in Year 3 reduces the cash surrender value, meaning that upon policy lapse, less or potentially nothing remains due to the deduction of fees and charges.</data>
  <data key="d4">reduces value</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b" target="1c5eba0f-2f29-43d1-b13a-bc342d4f4ae4">
  <data key="d3">A higher surrender charge in Year 3 could discourage early withdrawals despite favorable index account performance, potentially reducing the benefit derived from strong index-linked gains.</data>
  <data key="d4">contextual relevance</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b" target="e6aa2762-a82e-4371-9d8e-da19a25dd6d1">
  <data key="d3">A 8% surrender charge in Year 3 may reduce the effective return earned under the S&amp;P 500 Index Account, especially if the account has grown significantly over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">reduces net benefit</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b" target="62714aed-4640-40fa-9927-1e7eaaddb24c">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge of 8% in Year 3, specified in fact_sentence_2, affects any index account used in the policy, including the NASDAQ-100 Index Account detailed in fact_sentence_1, meaning the charge would impact returns generated through that particular index.</data>
  <data key="d4">contextual relationship</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b" target="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176">
  <data key="d3">A surrender charge of 8% in Year 3 depends on prior premium payments, reinforcing the importance of consistently paying at least $100 per installment to avoid losing significant portions of accumulated value when exiting early.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b" target="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2">
  <data key="d3">The 8% surrender charge in Year 3 reflects one consequence of paying high premiums within the allowable range, particularly affecting those who contribute near the $50,000 annual limit.</data>
  <data key="d4">financial implication</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b" target="0d35c1ce-d96d-4562-80f8-0654abe126d2">
  <data key="d3">An 8% surrender charge in Year 3 depends on the level of prior premiums paid, so exceeding the $50,000 annual cap would amplify these costs, though the cap itself ensures compliance with tax-qualified plan rules.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b" target="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d">
  <data key="d3">A 8% surrender charge in Year 3 underscores the importance of meeting the $6,000 annual premium recommendation to prevent premature policy termination and associated financial losses.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b" target="0b7e0a06-5166-489d-a873-3b798f915e2c">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges in Year 3 impact the final payout if the policyholder terminates the contract, reducing the effective return on accumulated funds that were already subject to monthly charges such as COI and administration fees.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences account value</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b" target="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 identifies a concrete surrender charge amount in Year 3, which supports understanding the financial implications referenced when switching death benefit options under the 60-day rule outlined in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">consistent with</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b" target="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5">
  <data key="d3">The 8% surrender charge in Year 3 reduces the surrender value, thereby lowering the upper limit of the 90% loan amount that can be taken against it.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b" target="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22">
  <data key="d3">The 8% surrender charge in Year 3 influences decisions about taking loans or withdrawing funds, especially considering that such actions may trigger higher out-of-pocket costs due to the net 1% loan expense.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b" target="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb">
  <data key="d3">The Year 3 surrender charge affects the amount received upon withdrawal or surrender, whereas the 1% net loan cost impacts long-term borrowing efficiency. Though distinct, both influence total policy economics and should be considered together when evaluating financial trade-offs.</data>
  <data key="d4">contextual relevance</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
