  <data key="d3">A surrender charge of 3% in Year 8 implies it was higher earlier, such as 10% in Year 1, showing a progressive reduction over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">increases from</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75" target="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890">
  <data key="d3">Year 8 occurs later than Year 2, so its lower surrender charge aligns with the gradual reduction schedule outlined in the chunk summary.</data>
  <data key="d4">follows and increases</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75" target="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b">
  <data key="d3">Year 8’s lower surrender charge (3%) follows logically from the gradual reduction beginning in Year 3, aligning with the annual decrease rule outlined in the summary.</data>
  <data key="d4">follows and is less than</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75" target="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 reports the surrender charge in Year 8 as 3%, which depends on the earlier charge in Year 4 being higher (7%) to demonstrate the ongoing reduction pattern across the first 12 years.</data>
  <data key="d4">follows and is lower than</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75" target="00111295-2bb8-4547-912d-c65ce0d8d633">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge decreases each year, so the lower rate in Year 8 logically follows from the higher rate observed in Year 5.</data>
  <data key="d4">follows</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75" target="84b84dec-45b7-4ca8-ae2f-a68466866f24">
  <data key="d3">Year 8’s surrender charge of 3% follows Year 6’s 5%, demonstrating the declining trend in charges across consecutive years as specified in the policy terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">follows</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75" target="29e19c25-f1c1-4c3e-8db6-46bce82c0dca">
  <data key="d3">Year 8’s surrender charge of 3% follows directly from the declining trend initiated in Year 7, maintaining consistency with the gradual elimination of charges over the first 12 years.</data>
  <data key="d4">follows</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75" target="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00">
  <data key="d3">Year 8’s surrender charge of 3% precedes and sets the context for Year 9’s lower rate of 2%, reflecting the scheduled annual reduction in fees.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75" target="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86">
  <data key="d3">Year 8's surrender charge of 3% fits into the gradual decline toward zero over 12 years, setting context for Year 11’s lower charge of 0.5%, which continues the established trend.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75" target="a3cf559b-392a-434d-8391-67212bc086c3">
  <data key="d3">Year 8's surrender charge of 3% fits into the gradual decline trend leading toward zero by Year 12. Fact_sentence_2 shows an even lower rate at Year 10, continuing this downward trajectory.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75" target="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73">
  <data key="d3">Year 8 occurs before Year 12, so the 3% surrender charge applies prior to the point at which charges fully expire. This reflects the gradual decline pattern over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75" target="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 8 being 3% aligns with the rule that charges are based on premiums paid within the first 10 years, showing an application of the general calculation principle.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75" target="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 8 is explicitly used in determining the cash surrender value by being subtracted from the account value along with any outstanding loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">used in calculation</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75" target="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a">
  <data key="d3">A surrender charge of 3% in Year 8 reduces the account value available at surrender or lapse. This reduction means less or potentially zero surrender value may remain when the policy lapses.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75" target="e6aa2762-a82e-4371-9d8e-da19a25dd6d1">
  <data key="d3">A 3% surrender charge in Year 8 reduces the net payout upon early termination, potentially affecting the attractiveness of holding the S&amp;P 500 Index Account long-term despite its return mechanism.</data>
  <data key="d4">moderated by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75" target="faf66c9e-da0e-4813-9561-2d1480419596">
  <data key="d3">A 3% surrender charge in Year 8 reduces net gains upon withdrawal, potentially offsetting some benefits of the 100% participation rate in the S&amp;P 500 account, especially if the policyholder exits before full benefit accrual.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75" target="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176">
  <data key="d3">A surrender charge of 3% in Year 8 underscores the importance of maintaining regular premium payments—at least $100—to build enough account value and avoid losing significant portions of contributions if withdrawn prematurely.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75" target="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d">
  <data key="d3">A 3% surrender charge in Year 8 implies that withdrawing funds early may reduce net returns, making consistent adherence to the $6,000 premium recommendation crucial for preserving long-term value.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75" target="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d">
  <data key="d3">The 3% surrender charge in Year 8 reflects a penalty tied to early termination, which interacts with prior payments—including those affected by the 3.5% premium load—that determine the net surrender value.</data>
  <data key="d4">moderated by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75" target="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f">
  <data key="d3">A 3% surrender charge in Year 8 may influence decisions about maintaining payments that fund monthly COI deductions, as higher fees could discourage early cancellation despite consistent premium contributions.</data>
  <data key="d4">moderated by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75" target="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5">
  <data key="d3">A lower surrender charge in Year 8 increases the effective surrender value, thereby expanding the pool from which the 90% maximum loan amount can be drawn.</data>
  <data key="d4">enhances</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75" target="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6">
  <data key="d3">A 3% surrender charge in Year 8 affects the net gain from holding the policy, especially when combined with the 4% loan interest rate, potentially reducing returns despite favorable investment performance.</data>
  <data key="d4">contextual relevance</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75" target="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22">
  <data key="d3">The Year 8 surrender charge of 3% reflects ongoing policy fees tied to early withdrawal, whereas the 3% fixed account rate applies only when funds are actively loaned. These two figures represent separate financial mechanisms affecting long-term value differently.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75" target="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb">
  <data key="d3">The 3% surrender charge in Year 8 complements the understanding of long-term policy costs, while the 1% net loan cost illustrates ongoing funding efficiency. Together, they inform decisions about withdrawal timing and debt management relative to policy duration.</data>
  <data key="d4">contextual relationship</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
