  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">concept</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e">
  <data key="d3">The 2% surrender charge in Year 9 exemplifies the broader rule that surrender charges decrease annually over the initial 12-year period.</data>
  <data key="d4">part of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018">
  <data key="d3">A surrender charge of 2% in Year 9 implies that earlier years had higher charges, such as the 10% rate in Year 1, demonstrating a progressive reduction over time within the 12-year window.</data>
  <data key="d4">increased from</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 9 is 2%, which follows from the gradual annual drop beginning at 10% in Year 1. Since Year 2 had a charge of 9%, it marks an earlier stage in the same downward trajectory.</data>
  <data key="d4">follows</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b">
  <data key="d3">The 2% surrender charge in Year 9 logically follows from the earlier 8% charge in Year 3, reflecting an ongoing annual decrease in surrender fees across the initial term.</data>
  <data key="d4">follows</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge decreases each year, so the lower charge in Year 9 (2%) logically follows from the higher charge in Year 4 (7%).</data>
  <data key="d4">increases from</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="00111295-2bb8-4547-912d-c65ce0d8d633">
  <data key="d3">Year 9’s lower surrender charge compared to Year 5 illustrates the ongoing reduction pattern established early in the policy lifecycle, where charges diminish steadily each year.</data>
  <data key="d4">follows</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="84b84dec-45b7-4ca8-ae2f-a68466866f24">
  <data key="d3">Since the surrender charge decreases every year, the lower rate in Year 9 logically follows from the higher rate observed in Year 6, maintaining continuity in the fee structure.</data>
  <data key="d4">follows</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="29e19c25-f1c1-4c3e-8db6-46bce82c0dca">
  <data key="d3">Year 9's lower surrender charge (2%) follows logically from the declining trend established in Year 7 (4%), demonstrating a sequential drop in fees over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">follows</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75">
  <data key="d3">Year 9’s reduced surrender charge of 2% builds upon the prior year’s higher charge of 3%, demonstrating an ongoing downward trend per the plan.</data>
  <data key="d4">follows</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86">
  <data key="d3">Year 9's surrender charge of 2% precedes and sets context for the lower charge in Year 11, illustrating the ongoing decline in fees across the initial term.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73">
  <data key="d3">Year 9 has a remaining surrender charge of 2%, reflecting its position before the final reduction to zero at Year 12. This indicates progression toward full elimination of charges by the end of the 12-year window.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df">
  <data key="d3">The 2% surrender charge in Year 9 is determined by applying the annual percentage rule to the total premiums paid within the initial ten-year window, consistent with the stated calculation basis.</data>
  <data key="d4">derives from</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="a3cf559b-392a-434d-8391-67212bc086c3">
  <data key="d3">Year 9's surrender charge of 2% logically precedes and leads into Year 10’s lower charge of 1%, reflecting the annual decline in surrender fees over time within the policy term.</data>
  <data key="d4">precedes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.98</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge in Year 9 being 2% is used as an input when calculating the cash surrender value. This specific rate affects the final value derived by subtracting it from the account value along with any outstanding loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">input dependency</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a">
  <data key="d3">A surrender charge of 2% in Year 9 reduces the account value available upon withdrawal or surrender. This reduction increases the likelihood that the remaining surrender value may be zero or negative if the policy lapses without sufficient funds.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="e6aa2762-a82e-4371-9d8e-da19a25dd6d1">
  <data key="d3">A 2% surrender charge in Year 9 may discourage early withdrawal, potentially influencing whether policyholders benefit fully from the S&amp;P 500 Index Account’s compounded gains over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">impacted by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176">
  <data key="d3">A $100 minimum premium enables sustained policy ownership through Year 9, ensuring eligibility for surrender charges only if the policyholder chooses to withdraw early rather than let it mature.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d">
  <data key="d3">A 2% surrender charge in Year 9 underscores why meeting the $6,000 annual recommendation is crucial—to minimize erosion of accumulated value upon early termination.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d">
  <data key="d3">The 2% surrender charge in Year 9 reflects a penalty tied to accumulated premiums, making it more costly to terminate the policy late in its term; however, since the 3.5% load already diminishes the effective premium contribution, the impact of the surrender charge is partially influenced by prior deductions.</data>
  <data key="d4">moderated by load</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f">
  <data key="d3">A 2% surrender charge in Year 9 impacts the final payout if the policyholder exits early, especially considering ongoing COI deductions have already lowered the account value over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="0b7e0a06-5166-489d-a873-3b798f915e2c">
  <data key="d3">A surrender charge in Year 9 impacts the final payout if the policyholder terminates it at that stage, meaning any accumulated funds less the surrender charge may reflect prior reductions due to monthly charges such as COI and administration fees.</data>
  <data key="d4">modulated by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25">
  <data key="d3">The Year 9 surrender charge of 2% reflects the ongoing decline in penalties throughout the policy’s early years, consistent with the conditions enabling changes like switching death benefit options, which require prior notification.</data>
  <data key="d4">related to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5">
  <data key="d3">A 2% surrender charge in Year 9 affects the net surrender value, thereby influencing the upper limit of possible policy loans, since loans cannot exceed 90% of the adjusted surrender value.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences limit</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22">
  <data key="d3">The Year 9 surrender charge of 2% fits into the broader timeline of diminishing fees, which impacts when borrowers might repay loans without significant penalty, especially considering loan interest accrual.</data>
  <data key="d4">contextualizes cost</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb">
  <data key="d3">The Year 9 surrender charge (2%) impacts the effective return on investment, indirectly influencing the overall cost-effectiveness of taking out a loan, especially if the policy is surrendered before maturity.</data>
  <data key="d4">contextual relationship</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00" target="9ac0c7c4-1321-469b-afaa-abe6d54dbd8e">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge detail in Year 9 is part of a policy governed by Horizon Wealth Protection Insurance, whose authority and authenticity are affirmed through documentation.</data>
  <data key="d4">source of policy</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
