  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a3cf559b-392a-434d-8391-67212bc086c3" target="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa">
  <data key="d3">A 1% surrender charge in Year 10 reflects a cost associated with exiting the policy early, which underscores the importance of meeting minimum premium obligations like the $100 requirement to build sufficient account value and avoid higher relative losses upon withdrawal.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a3cf559b-392a-434d-8391-67212bc086c3" target="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2">
  <data key="d3">The 1% surrender charge in Year 10 reflects a penalty tied to early withdrawal risk, which depends on accumulated premiums—including those capped at $50,000 annually—thus linking back to the upper limit on premium payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a3cf559b-392a-434d-8391-67212bc086c3" target="0d35c1ce-d96d-4562-80f8-0654abe126d2">
  <data key="d3">The 1% surrender charge in Year 10 depends on prior premium payments, which are capped at $50,000 annually under tax-qualified rules, thus linking the penalty directly to the maximum allowable contribution.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
