<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="e6aa2762-a82e-4371-9d8e-da19a25dd6d1">
  <data key="d3">A 0.5% surrender charge in Year 11 reduces the net proceeds from withdrawing funds, potentially diminishing gains accrued through the S&amp;P 500 Index Account.</data>
  <data key="d4">impacted by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa">
  <data key="d3">A 0.5% surrender charge in Year 11 underscores the importance of sustained premium payments, such as the $100 minimum, to prevent premature policy cancellation and associated financial losses.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="0d35c1ce-d96d-4562-80f8-0654abe126d2">
  <data key="d3">A 0.5% surrender charge in Year 11 reflects the diminishing penalties over time, allowing flexibility for high-premium contributors who may have reached the $50,000 annual cap under tax-qualified terms.</data>
  <data key="d4">supprts</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d">
  <data key="d3">A reduced surrender charge of 0.5% in Year 11 makes it financially less risky to exit the policy late in its term, supporting the feasibility of meeting the $6,000 annual premium goal without fear of high penalties.</data>
  <data key="d4">enhances feasibility</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="0b7e0a06-5166-489d-a873-3b798f915e2c">
  <data key="d3">A surrender charge in Year 11 reflects long-term policy withdrawal consequences, which depend on accumulated account value affected by consistent deductions such as monthly COI and administrative fees described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5">
  <data key="d3">A low surrender charge in Year 11 increases the surrender value, thereby enabling a larger maximum loan amount (up to 90%) compared to earlier years when charges were higher.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6">
  <data key="d3">A very low surrender charge of 0.5% in Year 11 makes it financially viable to repay or manage a 4% policy loan, minimizing the risk of losing equity due to surrender fees.</data>
  <data key="d4">financially compatible</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86" target="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb">
  <data key="d3">A consistent net borrowing cost of 1% per annum implies predictable financing costs, making it more financially viable to retain the policy into later years like Year 11, where surrender charges have significantly declined to 0.5%.</data>
  <data key="d4">enhances feasibility</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="1fca6732-8e76-4234-b407-99cc37e6696d" target="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">has surrender charge</data>
</edge>
