<edge source="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df" target="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e">
  <data key="d3">The calculation of surrender charges—as a percentage of early premiums—is only relevant because such charges are enforced when policies are surrendered within the first 12 years, making the time frame essential to applying the formula.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df" target="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018">
  <data key="d3">The general rule that surrender charges depend on early premium payments supports why the Year 1 charge is set at 10%, aligning with its annual reduction schedule.</data>
  <data key="d4">applies to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df" target="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890">
  <data key="d3">Since the surrender charge is calculated using premiums paid in the initial decade, it logically determines the exact amount—for example, 9% in Year 2—as part of an annual reduction schedule.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df" target="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b">
  <data key="d3">The general rule that surrender charges depend on premiums paid in the first 10 years directly supports why the charge in Year 3 is set at 8%.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df" target="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332">
  <data key="d3">The general rule that surrender charges are based on premiums paid in the first decade directly supports why the charge in Year 4 is set at 7%, ensuring consistency with the declining schedule over the initial 12-year period.</data>
  <data key="d4">derives from</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df" target="00111295-2bb8-4547-912d-c65ce0d8d633">
  <data key="d3">The general rule that surrender charges are based on premiums paid in the first decade supports why the charge in Year 5 is set at 6%, reflecting its position in the declining schedule.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df" target="84b84dec-45b7-4ca8-ae2f-a68466866f24">
  <data key="d3">Since the surrender charge in Year 6 is 5%, it confirms that the charge mechanism relies on premiums paid during the initial decade, validating the stated computation basis.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df" target="29e19c25-f1c1-4c3e-8db6-46bce82c0dca">
  <data key="d3">Since surrender charges decrease annually over 12 years and are tied to early premium payments, the specific charge of 4% in Year 7 logically follows from the stated calculation basis involving initial premiums.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df" target="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75">
  <data key="d3">The general rule that surrender charges depend on early premium payments supports why the charge in Year 8 is set at 3%, illustrating how the broader rule informs the specific case.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df" target="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00">
  <data key="d3">The general rule that surrender charges are based on premiums paid in the first 10 years supports why the charge in Year 9 is set at 2%, reflecting its position in the declining schedule tied to those early payments.</data>
  <data key="d4">applies to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df" target="a3cf559b-392a-434d-8391-67212bc086c3">
  <data key="d3">Since surrender charges decrease annually from 10% to 0% over the first decade, the specific instance of a 1% charge in Year 10 logically follows from being computed as a percentage of total premiums paid during that timeframe.</data>
  <data key="d4">derives from</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df" target="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86">
  <data key="d3">The calculation method for surrender charges—as a percentage of early premiums—is what determines why the charge in Year 11 amounts to 0.5%, linking the general rule to its specific instance.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df" target="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73">
  <data key="d3">Since surrender charges are tied to early premium payments, their gradual reduction culminates in a full exemption from Year 12 onward.</data>
  <data key="d4">causes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df" target="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge, determined by a percentage of premiums paid within the first ten years, is subtracted from the account value along with outstanding loans to compute the cash surrender value.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df" target="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge calculation method informs when fees may apply, enabling clarity around why certain withdrawals remain free even if surrender charges exist otherwise.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df" target="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges reduce the potential surrender value, so when a policy lapses due to non-payment, the accumulated value—already diminished by those charges—is fully forfeited.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df" target="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges being applied to premiums paid within the first 10 years depend on those payments meeting the minimum threshold of $100 per installment, reinforcing the importance of the minimum payment rule.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df" target="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges applied in the first 10 years depend on cumulative premiums paid, making the $100 minimum payment relevant to potential future penalties.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df" target="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges based on early-year premiums affect the net return on contributions capped at $50,000 annually, influencing long-term financial planning around premium levels.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df" target="0d35c1ce-d96d-4562-80f8-0654abe126d2">
  <data key="d3">Higher annual premiums capped at $50,000 contribute more toward surrender charges in the initial ten years, influencing overall policy cost efficiency.</data>
  <data key="d4">impacted by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df" target="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges applied in the first 10 years depend on total premiums paid, making sustained adherence to the $6,000 recommendation financially prudent to minimize future exit penalties.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.78</data>
</edge>
<edge source="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df" target="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges depend on premiums paid in the first 10 years, so the consistent application of a 3.5% load per payment increases the cumulative premiums subject to these charges.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df" target="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges reduce the net cash surrender value, potentially limiting the funds available to cover future Cost of Insurance payments, especially if policyholder actions lead to lapses.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df" target="0b7e0a06-5166-489d-a873-3b798f915e2c">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges depend on early-year premiums, so consistent payments reduce future surrender penalties, indirectly supporting sustained coverage despite ongoing monthly deductions.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df" target="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges being calculated on premiums paid in the first 10 years provide context for why early changes to death benefit options may carry significant financial implications, reinforcing the need for timely planning such as the 60-day notice rule.</data>
  <data key="d4">informs</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df" target="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges, derived from premiums paid in the first decade, influence the surrender value, thereby impacting the upper limit of allowable policy loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df" target="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges based on early premiums impact the feasibility of accessing funds via withdrawal or loan, making high-cost borrowing less attractive relative to the 4% loan rate.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df" target="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22">
  <data key="d3">Surrender charges based on premiums paid affect the effective cost of exiting the policy early, indirectly influencing decisions about taking loans, which carry a net cost due to the difference between loan interest and fixed account returns.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df" target="9ac0c7c4-1321-469b-afaa-abe6d54dbd8e">
  <data key="d3">The surrender charge mechanism described in fact_sentence_1 is governed by the policies of Horizon Wealth Protection Insurance, whose identity is confirmed in fact_sentence_2, providing organizational context for the rule.</data>
  <data key="d4">contextual link</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
