<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="4392497f-15c1-48ee-8067-43a8245bc89e">
  <data key="d3">The formula for calculating the cash surrender value includes the deduction of surrender charges, meaning that such charges must be present or applicable for the computation to reflect accurate values under early surrender scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d4">used in</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="01ec375d-e72b-4c13-96a2-da5a23238018">
  <data key="d3">The cash surrender value formula depends on the surrender charge amount—such as the 10% charge in Year 1—to determine the net payout upon withdrawal or surrender.</data>
  <data key="d4">used in calculation</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="9dcea0cf-204b-429a-93cc-c257133b7890">
  <data key="d3">The cash surrender value depends on subtracting the surrender charge from the account value, meaning the 9% surrender charge in Year 2 directly affects the resulting cash surrender value.</data>
  <data key="d4">used in calculation of</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="273e0e6e-5536-4336-a312-2596a9f16c8b">
  <data key="d3">The formula for cash surrender value depends on knowing the current surrender charge—such as the 8% charge in Year 3—to accurately compute its final value.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences value</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="5935cab6-342e-4e3e-9ea8-dbff499af332">
  <data key="d3">The formula for cash surrender value includes the surrender charge, so knowing that the charge in Year 4 is 7% allows accurate computation of the cash surrender value at that time.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences value</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="00111295-2bb8-4547-912d-c65ce0d8d633">
  <data key="d3">The formula for cash surrender value requires subtracting the surrender charge—such as the 6% charge in Year 5—to determine the net payout. Therefore, the definition relies on having a known surrender charge figure like that stated in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">used in</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="84b84dec-45b7-4ca8-ae2f-a68466866f24">
  <data key="d3">The cash surrender value depends on subtracting the surrender charge—such as the 5% charge in Year 6—from the account value and any outstanding loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences value</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="29e19c25-f1c1-4c3e-8db6-46bce82c0dca">
  <data key="d3">The formula for cash surrender value includes deducting the surrender charge, so knowing the exact charge—such as 4% in Year 7—is essential for determining the final cash surrender value.</data>
  <data key="d4">input to formula</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="e9e8f00a-1414-40a5-99b4-1975b3ddee75">
  <data key="d3">The formula for calculating the cash surrender value includes the surrender charge, so knowing the specific charge in Year 8 allows accurate computation of that value.</data>
  <data key="d4">informs value</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="fe831b43-8690-4c01-9873-79e0ef24ae00">
  <data key="d3">The formula for cash surrender value includes deducting the surrender charge, so knowing that the charge is 2% in Year 9 allows accurate computation of the actual surrender value under those conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">used in calculation</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="a3cf559b-392a-434d-8391-67212bc086c3">
  <data key="d3">The formula for cash surrender value includes deducting the surrender charge, such as the 1% charge in Year 10, from the account value before accounting for other liabilities like outstanding loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">used in calculation</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="b29caae3-f13a-4b43-af52-606c74d4bb86">
  <data key="d3">The cash surrender value depends on subtracting the surrender charge—such as the 0.5% charge in Year 11—from the account value, meaning the exact charge amount determines the resulting cash value.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences result</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="8581e6b9-7fac-4b65-a5c3-f8bf614bbe73">
  <data key="d3">The definition of cash surrender value includes deducting surrender charges, so if those charges are zero in Year 12 or beyond, the resulting cash surrender value increases accordingly—directly supporting the claim made in fact_sentence_1 about zero charges.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="120104c2-987f-4f54-a944-5d235a6dd5df">
  <data key="d3">To calculate the cash surrender value, the surrender charge—derived from premiums paid in the initial decade—is deducted from the account value alongside any outstanding loans.</data>
  <data key="d4">used in</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="9d636a77-9852-432c-b8fb-7593d751a2da">
  <data key="d3">The cash surrender value, determined by subtracting surrender charges and loans from the account value, represents the net amount available for withdrawals. This directly supports the policyholder’s eligibility to make annual partial withdrawals up to 10% of the account value.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b">
  <data key="d3">The formula for Cash Surrender Value includes deducting surrender charges, but partial withdrawals after Year 1 occur without those charges, meaning they do not reduce the surrender value via surrender fees.</data>
  <data key="d4">exempt from</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="fed316a6-229f-46af-91a9-72511967565a">
  <data key="d3">The calculation of Cash Surrender Value includes subtracting surrender charges and loans from the account value. After a policy lapse, any such surrendered value becomes forfeited, meaning it cannot be recovered.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="1b43685f-2a0d-488f-9258-b0a8a87ea9f1">
  <data key="d3">A higher account value resulting from consistent indexing (supported by the 4% cap) increases the potential Cash Surrender Value, making the credit cap an indirect contributor to surrender benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences account value</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7">
  <data key="d3">The formula for Cash Surrender Value depends on the account’s accumulated value, which includes benefits from the 25% minimum participation rate on indexed credits, making the crediting rule relevant to final surrender payouts.</data>
  <data key="d4">related to</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="c4dbdf51-a4cd-4a65-8903-f269d529eefd">
  <data key="d3">The cash surrender value formula includes deductions that reduce net payouts, meaning even though the fixed account offers a stable 2% return, actual take-home amounts depend on surrender charges and loan balances.</data>
  <data key="d4">subject to constraints</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="1d4b712e-5e26-4cf9-a7ad-301c683e58e3">
  <data key="d3">Cash Surrender Value reflects the net worth of the policy at withdrawal, influenced by factors such as accumulated account value affected by the Cap Rate’s ceiling on indexed growth.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences value</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="a3259e6d-b7fd-4e82-92f7-523ed8d8a955">
  <data key="d3">The Cash Surrender Value depends on the Account Value, which is influenced by the Participation Rate’s contribution to index-linked growth over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="42ce1796-4b22-4fa1-987f-341d1746d7f3">
  <data key="d3">Cash Surrender Value depends on the Account Value, which is influenced by the Point-to-Point Method’s annual interest crediting process.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="e6aa2762-a82e-4371-9d8e-da19a25dd6d1">
  <data key="d3">The formula for cash surrender value includes deductions affecting net account value, which reflects the impact of index-based gains/losses such as those governed by the S&amp;P 500's point-to-point method.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="492399d4-a4a8-470a-b04c-a4e38ca316d2">
  <data key="d3">Cash surrender value incorporates account value adjustments that may reflect capped returns from indices like the S&amp;P 500, meaning the 10.5% cap could limit the maximum increase in account value impacting the final cash surrender amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences value</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="faf66c9e-da0e-4813-9561-2d1480419596">
  <data key="d3">Higher Account Values resulting from full participation in the S&amp;P 500 Index enhance the basis for determining Cash Surrender Value, making the participation rate indirectly influential on payout outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="a0671d34-e31b-4b17-8ed5-6a9d495c5148">
  <data key="d3">The Cash Surrender Value formula depends on the Account Value, which accumulates based on annual crediting periods such as the one-year cycle specified for the S&amp;P 500 Index Account in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="62714aed-4640-40fa-9927-1e7eaaddb24c">
  <data key="d3">Cash Surrender Value calculations depend on the Account Value generated by index accounts such as the NASDAQ-100, making the index mechanism relevant to final payout potential.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="32909f74-b806-4169-8ab1-602ea158ef9f">
  <data key="d3">The cash surrender value formula relies on the account value, which is impacted by the 100% participation rate in the NASDAQ-100 Index Account, meaning higher returns under that mechanism increase the base value used in calculating surrender benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="b0213eb9-bcd3-41f0-9381-ae8e81ac0f24">
  <data key="d3">The Cash Surrender Value formula depends on the account's accumulated value, influenced by annual crediting periods such as the 1-year cycle used for the NASDAQ-100 Index Account.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="de64be79-d83e-496d-97f6-5d2e80705c21">
  <data key="d3">Cash Surrender Value depends on the account’s total value, which includes returns generated by index accounts like the Global Diversified Index Account. Therefore, changes in the indexed account directly affect the basis for calculating surrender value.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="13cdba53-929e-487b-9dac-c7e31bdd92a0">
  <data key="d3">The cash surrender value formula subtracts surrender charges and loans from the account value, meaning any increase in account value driven by the 8.5% cap on the Global Diversified Index Account would indirectly affect the final cash surrender amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">impacted by cap rate</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="22fdc352-4139-456b-bd73-2207bfdefc4e">
  <data key="d3">The Cash Surrender Value formula relies on the Account Value, which is impacted by the 100% Participation Rate in the Global Diversified Index Account. Thus, high participation enhances account value and indirectly increases surrender benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">impacted by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="7d3930c1-6b23-4a04-93b3-d874c9e7b176">
  <data key="d3">The formula for calculating cash surrender value includes the account value, which is built through periodic premium payments—each of which must meet the $100 minimum specified in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="44171d39-27ff-4fcc-bf40-58a3e92080fa">
  <data key="d3">The formula for cash surrender value includes deductions that depend on accumulated premiums; thus, maintaining at least the $100 minimum ensures sufficient account growth to support meaningful surrender values later.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="b8046f06-ce88-4546-bb7c-16ba4c69bcf2">
  <data key="d3">The formula for cash surrender value includes deductions that depend on accumulated premiums, making the $50,000 annual premium limit relevant to its final amount.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="0d35c1ce-d96d-4562-80f8-0654abe126d2">
  <data key="d3">The formula for cash surrender value depends on accumulated account value, which is influenced by annual payments capped at $50,000. Thus, the upper limit on premiums constrains the maximum possible account value used in determining surrender benefits.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.78</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="c0561218-4570-4bd7-925f-25cc01fd0c6d">
  <data key="d3">The cash surrender value calculation relies on the account value, which accumulates based on consistent premium payments such as the recommended $6,000 per year stated in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="0d7fabe2-d74d-4b84-a620-42c9acb1c43d">
  <data key="d3">The cash surrender value depends on the account value, which is diminished by the 3.5% load applied to every premium payment, making the load a contributing factor in its determination.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences base value</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="e4d325d0-3102-4ecf-b8a5-e488e84fa28f">
  <data key="d3">The Cash Surrender Value formula depends on the account value, which is reduced over time by recurring expenses like the monthly Cost of Insurance charge described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="1b6d4d68-07ed-4c80-987c-ddf958d36f08">
  <data key="d3">The cash surrender value depends on the account value after deductions like those made on the third day of every month.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="52cae3fa-7111-45dd-93a0-0249fc2b3e25">
  <data key="d3">The formula for cash surrender value includes surrender charges and loans, which are relevant when switching death benefit options requiring 60-day notice, especially given that such changes may trigger loan activity or alter surrender implications.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="e35519d3-d4b6-4a91-b9cc-794ecf0231f5">
  <data key="d3">The surrender value used to calculate the maximum loan amount (90%) is determined by subtracting both surrender charges and existing loans from the account value, meaning prior loans affect the base figure for future borrowing capacity.</data>
  <data key="d4">informs</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="84b477e8-9a8c-4a97-b7ac-12df058493f6">
  <data key="d3">The formula for cash surrender value includes outstanding loans, so the 4% interest charged on those loans accumulates over time, diminishing the actual cash proceeds available upon surrender.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="d39b66e7-d38a-450c-a287-bd1bf0a73d22">
  <data key="d3">The fixed account's 3% earnings on loans help offset the cost of borrowing, but since loans reduce the cash surrender value, the actual economic gain depends on how much is repaid versus what remains owed when the policy ends.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="16db743e-8a3d-4763-8527-b5d06fd8aafb">
  <data key="d3">The definition of cash surrender value includes outstanding loans, which directly affect the effective cost of borrowing, thereby grounding the 1% net cost mentioned in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="cdffaf84-8d6b-4f83-8142-43784e03289a">
  <data key="d3">The reduction in cash surrender value due to outstanding loans, as stated here, supports why such loans lower the death benefit when claims occur.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="9ac0c7c4-1321-469b-afaa-abe6d54dbd8e">
  <data key="d3">The calculation of Cash Surrender Value depends on policies governed by Horizon Wealth Protection Insurance, whose identity confirms the source of the financial rules outlined in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">contextual support</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a" target="79f032d3-1299-41de-85c7-f944c1411556">
  <data key="d3">The cash surrender value formula applies to policies active at the time of document execution on October 3, 2024, ensuring that the defined calculations remain relevant under current conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">temporal context</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="0434ff4e-d322-4d7c-afd5-e0b3a3c3eaf3" target="8e4cefcc-7f56-4cf2-9f4b-3e5dc497847a">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
