<edge source="c9695180-7458-48f9-8686-914a2e999aa0" target="7011576a-0546-4f50-af7e-9f414262d88b">
  <data key="d3">The No Lapse Guarantee Rider ensures continuous coverage even if the account value reaches zero, offering security against lapses. This stability supports the ability to take advantage of free partial withdrawals without fear of losing coverage.</data>
  <data key="d4">enhances</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9695180-7458-48f9-8686-914a2e999aa0" target="628900ad-3981-4384-be18-2669a41ba276">
  <data key="d3">The availability of the No Lapse Guarantee Rider allows policyholders to maintain coverage under adverse financial conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9695180-7458-48f9-8686-914a2e999aa0" target="59735a62-be54-4b86-a006-cd569871d4ef">
  <data key="d3">The No Lapse Guarantee Rider ensures continued coverage despite a zero account value, but only if minimum guaranteed premiums are consistently paid.</data>
  <data key="d4">conditional dependency</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="c9695180-7458-48f9-8686-914a2e999aa0" target="ae3f8271-673d-4549-8f9b-46011b263dfc">
  <data key="d3">The existence of a no-lapse guarantee rider would prevent policy lapse despite low account values, but since it wasn’t selected, its protective effect doesn’t apply. Therefore, the risk of lapse due to missed payments remains active.</data>
  <data key="d4">contradicts</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
