  <data key="d3">The statement that the policy is not a securities product sets the context for understanding its structural differences from financial instruments. This helps explain why index participation does not imply actual stock ownership, reinforcing the product’s non-investment character.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6e42de55-cde0-435f-b499-10c6b12172e2" target="2ec53e58-1461-418f-af0f-33f4dab5f971">
  <data key="d3">The statement that the policy is not a securities product supports the clarification that index participation involves no direct ownership of index funds, reinforcing the distinction between insurance features and traditional investments.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6e42de55-cde0-435f-b499-10c6b12172e2" target="5ba693f1-db68-45ea-a535-eef1cf763796">
  <data key="d3">The statement that the policy is not a securities product sets its regulatory category, providing context for why it includes disclaimers like the one about past performance not predicting future results.</data>
  <data key="d4">contextualizes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6e42de55-cde0-435f-b499-10c6b12172e2" target="b080d9ad-b053-459f-8150-83b862b99de1">
  <data key="d3">The statement that the policy is not a securities product provides context on its regulatory status, while the assurance that cap rates won't fall below guaranteed levels highlights built-in protection against market downturns. Together, they reinforce the product’s safety profile but operate independently.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6e42de55-cde0-435f-b499-10c6b12172e2" target="47fe3387-29bc-4869-a3a5-637bc22b6a91">
  <data key="d3">The statement that the policy is not a securities product provides foundational clarity on its regulatory status, supporting the broader claim that it offers zero downside risk by design.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6e42de55-cde0-435f-b499-10c6b12172e2" target="af34274c-dfee-4fb4-a491-3e2e93de0364">
  <data key="d3">The statement that the policy is not a securities product provides context on its regulatory nature, while the assurance of minimum guaranteed rates highlights financial safety nets. Together, they reinforce trust through clarity on product type and rate stability.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6e42de55-cde0-435f-b499-10c6b12172e2" target="05f6ec15-bbb6-4acf-8ed9-90e66f40d069">
  <data key="d3">The statement that the policy is not a securities product sets the context for understanding its regulatory framework. This helps explain why it includes built-in protections like a zero downside risk feature tied to index performance.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="6e42de55-cde0-435f-b499-10c6b12172e2" target="4323367b-0222-42cb-99fe-8a2785ec96d3">
  <data key="d3">The statement that the policy is not a securities product provides context for understanding its regulatory framework, while the detail about no dividend participation during negative index periods highlights a key limitation on benefits. Together, they reinforce transparency regarding investment characteristics and risks.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
