<edge source="7e3f4dce-a967-443e-8c1e-f4c1a24f502c" target="d95da1e8-f071-414b-b0ad-9b56d2f0e759">
  <data key="d3">Annual adjustments to participation rates affect how effectively index gains translate into benefits, regardless of the lack of actual stock ownership.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7e3f4dce-a967-443e-8c1e-f4c1a24f502c" target="2ec53e58-1461-418f-af0f-33f4dab5f971">
  <data key="d3">Annual changes in participation rates affect how effectively index gains translate into policy benefits, even though participants do not own underlying index funds directly.</data>
  <data key="d4">influences</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7e3f4dce-a967-443e-8c1e-f4c1a24f502c" target="a416fa11-2b3f-4f38-958d-ff8e13bcbb1a">
  <data key="d3">The potential annual fluctuation in participation rates is limited by a guaranteed minimum threshold, preventing any rate reduction below this baseline.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7e3f4dce-a967-443e-8c1e-f4c1a24f502c" target="b080d9ad-b053-459f-8150-83b862b99de1">
  <data key="d3">Changes in participation rates could affect cap rate calculations, but they are constrained by guaranteed minimums, ensuring stability regardless of market conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7e3f4dce-a967-443e-8c1e-f4c1a24f502c" target="05f6ec15-bbb6-4acf-8ed9-90e66f40d069">
  <data key="d3">The possibility of fluctuating participation rates affects how gains are allocated, yet the policy still protects against losses through guaranteed minimums regardless of market downturns.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7e3f4dce-a967-443e-8c1e-f4c1a24f502c" target="af34274c-dfee-4fb4-a491-3e2e93de0364">
  <data key="d3">The possibility of changing participation rates reflects adjustments in how funds are distributed across investment options, whereas fixed account rates remain protected by guaranteed floors. These statements address different mechanisms of rate management—one dynamic, one static—within the same policy framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7e3f4dce-a967-443e-8c1e-f4c1a24f502c" target="5ba693f1-db68-45ea-a535-eef1cf763796">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 indicates that participation rates can vary yearly, affecting how gains are allocated. This variability underscores why past performance should not be relied upon when predicting future outcomes, supporting the caution expressed in fact_sentence_2.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="7e3f4dce-a967-443e-8c1e-f4c1a24f502c" target="4323367b-0222-42cb-99fe-8a2785ec96d3">
  <data key="d3">If the index shows negative performance, the policyholder forfeits any dividend participation regardless of the current participation rate. This limits the impact of variable participation rates under adverse market conditions.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
