</edge>
<edge source="b080d9ad-b053-459f-8150-83b862b99de1" target="6e42de55-cde0-435f-b499-10c6b12172e2">
  <data key="d3">Guaranteed minimum cap rates ensure stable returns regardless of market conditions, supporting investor confidence. This feature complements the clarification that the product is not a security by reinforcing its conservative design and lack of exposure to typical investment volatility.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b080d9ad-b053-459f-8150-83b862b99de1" target="d95da1e8-f071-414b-b0ad-9b56d2f0e759">
  <data key="d3">Guaranteed minimum cap rates protect against extreme drops in index performance, which complements the clarification that participants do not own underlying stocks directly.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b080d9ad-b053-459f-8150-83b862b99de1" target="a6b58496-e890-407d-99f3-f8e86cce69dd">
  <data key="d3">Guaranteed minimums prevent cap rates from decreasing beyond a set threshold, thereby capping the extent of any decline even when annual revisions occur.</data>
  <data key="d4">constrains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b080d9ad-b053-459f-8150-83b862b99de1" target="7e3f4dce-a967-443e-8c1e-f4c1a24f502c">
  <data key="d3">Even if participation rates fluctuate annually, cap rates cannot drop below predetermined minimum levels, providing protection against extreme declines.</data>
  <data key="d4">constrains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b080d9ad-b053-459f-8150-83b862b99de1" target="09f59f75-d8f5-4cf9-b763-8e9b77770ca0">
  <data key="d3">Even though cap rates cannot drop below guaranteed minimums, fixed account rates remain subject to annual adjustments, reflecting separate mechanisms for rate management.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b080d9ad-b053-459f-8150-83b862b99de1" target="a416fa11-2b3f-4f38-958d-ff8e13bcbb1a">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee that cap rates won't fall below minimums supports the broader assurance that participation rates also remain protected at their guaranteed floors, reinforcing consistent policyholder benefits regardless of market volatility.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b080d9ad-b053-459f-8150-83b862b99de1" target="af34274c-dfee-4fb4-a491-3e2e93de0364">
  <data key="d3">Cap rates being protected by guaranteed minimums ensure that upside growth cannot exceed set ceilings, while fixed account rates maintain stability through floor protections. These clauses operate independently within distinct parts of the policy’s structure.</data>
  <data key="d4">parallel protection</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b080d9ad-b053-459f-8150-83b862b99de1" target="5ba693f1-db68-45ea-a535-eef1cf763796">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_1 establishes a floor for potential gains through guaranteed minimums, reinforcing stability. This supports the broader disclosure in fact_sentence_2 by illustrating why past performance alone cannot reliably indicate future success—since even under poor market conditions, returns won't drop below set thresholds.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b080d9ad-b053-459f-8150-83b862b99de1" target="47fe3387-29bc-4869-a3a5-637bc22b6a91">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee that cap rates won't drop below minimums supports the notion that zero represents a safe floor, making it central to risk protection. This structural safeguard enables the claim that zero acts as a protector against loss.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b080d9ad-b053-459f-8150-83b862b99de1" target="05f6ec15-bbb6-4acf-8ed9-90e66f40d069">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of minimum cap rates ensures that policyholders are protected against negative index movements, directly enabling the feature where they cannot lose money regardless of market downturns.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b080d9ad-b053-459f-8150-83b862b99de1" target="4323367b-0222-42cb-99fe-8a2785ec96d3">
  <data key="d3">The guaranteed minimum rate protects against extreme downturns, but even with such safeguards, the policyholder forfeits dividend benefits when the underlying index performs negatively.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b080d9ad-b053-459f-8150-83b862b99de1" target="f64306b3-60d7-48b6-82c2-6580397642e1">
  <data key="d3">Guaranteed minimum cap rates prevent reductions even under adverse conditions, directly enabling the 0% floor feature by ensuring structural stability in the indexing mechanism.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b080d9ad-b053-459f-8150-83b862b99de1" target="1b43685f-2a0d-488f-9258-b0a8a87ea9f1">
  <data key="d3">The claim that cap rates won't fall below guaranteed minimums underpins the assertion in fact_sentence_1 that caps will always remain at least 4%, showing that the numerical threshold is part of a larger system of protections.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b080d9ad-b053-459f-8150-83b862b99de1" target="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7">
  <data key="d3">Guaranteed minimum cap rates ensure that even under poor market conditions, the maximum potential credit remains above a threshold, which complements the floor on participation rates preventing any reduction below 25%.</data>
  <data key="d4">enhances</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="b080d9ad-b053-459f-8150-83b862b99de1" target="c4dbdf51-a4cd-4a65-8903-f269d529eefd">
  <data key="d3">The rule preventing cap rates from falling below guaranteed minimums supports the reliability of the fixed account’s 2% floor by maintaining consistent structural safeguards throughout the product design.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.92</data>
</edge>
<edge source="9d350918-7cd2-46a8-a798-4aad80fe7239" target="b080d9ad-b053-459f-8150-83b862b99de1">
  <data key="d2">entity_fact</data>
  <data key="d4">has guaranteed minimum</data>
</edge>
