  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">location</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a416fa11-2b3f-4f38-958d-ff8e13bcbb1a" target="ed304144-4e0f-416d-84a6-460f04f542a1">
  <data key="d2">fact_entity</data>
  <data key="d4">person</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a416fa11-2b3f-4f38-958d-ff8e13bcbb1a" target="e27b0a94-4088-4246-ba72-d6793b6cd04d">
  <data key="d3">Guaranteed minimum participation rates ensure stable returns even during poor market performance, reinforcing the policyholder’s ability to maintain coverage during periods like those covered by the grace period.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a416fa11-2b3f-4f38-958d-ff8e13bcbb1a" target="d95da1e8-f071-414b-b0ad-9b56d2f0e759">
  <data key="d3">Guaranteed minimum participation rates provide a safety net for those who do not own underlying stocks directly, maintaining value protection despite indirect exposure.</data>
  <data key="d4">enhances</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a416fa11-2b3f-4f38-958d-ff8e13bcbb1a" target="2ec53e58-1461-418f-af0f-33f4dab5f971">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee that participation rates won’t fall below minimum levels implies that the mechanism relies on indirect exposure rather than direct investment in index funds.</data>
  <data key="d4">justified by</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a416fa11-2b3f-4f38-958d-ff8e13bcbb1a" target="a6b58496-e890-407d-99f3-f8e86cce69dd">
  <data key="d3">Even if cap rates fluctuate annually, participation rates cannot drop below set minimum levels, maintaining baseline performance expectations.</data>
  <data key="d4">protects</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a416fa11-2b3f-4f38-958d-ff8e13bcbb1a" target="7e3f4dce-a967-443e-8c1e-f4c1a24f502c">
  <data key="d3">Guaranteed minimum participation rates ensure that even if annual adjustments occur, the rates cannot decrease beyond a specified lower bound.</data>
  <data key="d4">constrains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a416fa11-2b3f-4f38-958d-ff8e13bcbb1a" target="09f59f75-d8f5-4cf9-b763-8e9b77770ca0">
  <data key="d3">Guaranteed minimum participation rates provide a safety net regardless of fluctuations in fixed account rates, maintaining baseline benefits even when those rates change.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a416fa11-2b3f-4f38-958d-ff8e13bcbb1a" target="b080d9ad-b053-459f-8150-83b862b99de1">
  <data key="d3">Since participation rates are shielded by guaranteed minimums, this protection aligns with the mechanism ensuring cap rates do not drop below set thresholds, collectively preserving predictable returns.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a416fa11-2b3f-4f38-958d-ff8e13bcbb1a" target="af34274c-dfee-4fb4-a491-3e2e93de0364">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 1 states that participation rates are protected by guaranteed minimums, ensuring stable returns tied to underlying indexes. This supports the broader assurance of consistent performance mentioned in fact sentence 2 regarding fixed account rates.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a416fa11-2b3f-4f38-958d-ff8e13bcbb1a" target="5ba693f1-db68-45ea-a535-eef1cf763796">
  <data key="d3">The statement about guaranteed minimum participation rates underscores protection against poor performance, while the warning about past performance not predicting future results reinforces caution in interpreting historical data. Together, they frame a balanced view of expected returns under varying market scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a416fa11-2b3f-4f38-958d-ff8e13bcbb1a" target="05f6ec15-bbb6-4acf-8ed9-90e66f40d069">
  <data key="d3">The guaranteed minimum participation rate prevents any reduction below set thresholds, directly enabling the assurance that policyholders won't suffer financial loss from poor index performance.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a416fa11-2b3f-4f38-958d-ff8e13bcbb1a" target="47fe3387-29bc-4869-a3a5-637bc22b6a91">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of minimum participation rates underscores the policy’s design to prevent loss, directly supporting the notion that zero represents a safe outcome by eliminating downside risk.</data>
  <data key="d4">exemplifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a416fa11-2b3f-4f38-958d-ff8e13bcbb1a" target="4323367b-0222-42cb-99fe-8a2785ec96d3">
  <data key="d3">The guaranteed minimum participation rate ensures stability in policyholder benefits regardless of index performance, but when the index declines, no dividends are distributed despite the protection against loss.</data>
  <data key="d4">modifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a416fa11-2b3f-4f38-958d-ff8e13bcbb1a" target="f64306b3-60d7-48b6-82c2-6580397642e1">
  <data key="d3">Guaranteed minimum participation rates support the effectiveness of the 0% floor by ensuring meaningful credit even in flat markets, maintaining the integrity of the loss protection feature.</data>
  <data key="d4">depends on</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a416fa11-2b3f-4f38-958d-ff8e13bcbb1a" target="1b43685f-2a0d-488f-9258-b0a8a87ea9f1">
  <data key="d3">Guaranteed minimum participation rates support the stability of credited returns, which aligns with the hard ceiling of 4% being maintained across market cycles, ensuring predictable performance bounds.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a416fa11-2b3f-4f38-958d-ff8e13bcbb1a" target="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 affirms that participation rates cannot fall below guaranteed levels, thereby reinforcing the specificity of fact_sentence_1’s assertion that such rates will always remain at least 25%.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="a416fa11-2b3f-4f38-958d-ff8e13bcbb1a" target="c4dbdf51-a4cd-4a65-8903-f269d529eefd">
  <data key="d3">Guaranteed minimum participation rates support the broader framework of investor protections, which includes the fixed account’s unchanging 2% minimum return, reinforcing consistent expected performance.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
