<edge source="af34274c-dfee-4fb4-a491-3e2e93de0364" target="6e42de55-cde0-435f-b499-10c6b12172e2">
  <data key="d3">Guaranteed floor on fixed account rates underscores financial reliability, supporting the broader claim that the product carries minimal downside risk—a point reinforced by stating it’s not a securities product, thus avoiding market volatility exposure.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="af34274c-dfee-4fb4-a491-3e2e93de0364" target="7e3f4dce-a967-443e-8c1e-f4c1a24f502c">
  <data key="d3">Guaranteed minimums ensure stable returns in fixed accounts regardless of market conditions, providing a baseline against which fluctuating participation rates in variable accounts should be evaluated. This contrast highlights complementary safeguards in the policy’s design.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="af34274c-dfee-4fb4-a491-3e2e93de0364" target="09f59f75-d8f5-4cf9-b763-8e9b77770ca0">
  <data key="d3">Guaranteed minimums ensure that even if fixed account rates adjust downward annually, they remain protected from falling below a specified threshold.</data>
  <data key="d4">constrains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="af34274c-dfee-4fb4-a491-3e2e93de0364" target="b080d9ad-b053-459f-8150-83b862b99de1">
  <data key="d3">Fixed account rates are safeguarded against decline via guaranteed minimums, ensuring stable returns regardless of market conditions. This protection parallels cap rate guarantees, though applied to a separate mechanism within the policy framework.</data>
  <data key="d4">parallel protection</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="af34274c-dfee-4fb4-a491-3e2e93de0364" target="a416fa11-2b3f-4f38-958d-ff8e13bcbb1a">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 confirms that fixed account rates cannot drop below guaranteed levels, providing foundational reliability. This complements fact sentence 1’s guarantee on participation rates, collectively strengthening the policy's promise of minimal risk exposure.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="af34274c-dfee-4fb4-a491-3e2e93de0364" target="47fe3387-29bc-4869-a3a5-637bc22b6a91">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee that fixed account rates won't fall below minimums supports the broader concept of zero downside risk, reinforcing why "zero" symbolizes safety and reliability in risk protection.</data>
  <data key="d4">enhances</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="af34274c-dfee-4fb4-a491-3e2e93de0364" target="5ba693f1-db68-45ea-a535-eef1cf763796">
  <data key="d3">The assurance that fixed account rates won't drop below guaranteed levels provides a stable foundation, while the disclaimer about past performance not predicting future results reinforces cautious interpretation of historical data.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="af34274c-dfee-4fb4-a491-3e2e93de0364" target="05f6ec15-bbb6-4acf-8ed9-90e66f40d069">
  <data key="d3">The guarantee of minimum fixed account rates ensures that policyholders are protected against loss, enabling the zero downside risk claim when index performance declines.</data>
  <data key="d4">enables</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="af34274c-dfee-4fb4-a491-3e2e93de0364" target="f64306b3-60d7-48b6-82c2-6580397642e1">
  <data key="d3">Guaranteed minimum rates in the fixed account support the broader design principle seen in the 0% floor of the indexed account, emphasizing consistent risk protection throughout the product's structure.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="af34274c-dfee-4fb4-a491-3e2e93de0364" target="1b43685f-2a0d-488f-9258-b0a8a87ea9f1">
  <data key="d3">The assurance that index caps will never go below 4% complements the fixed account's guaranteed rate floor, collectively protecting investors from loss under varying market scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="af34274c-dfee-4fb4-a491-3e2e93de0364" target="0f6b3b49-d7b3-4758-a638-6cbce563fda7">
  <data key="d3">Guaranteed minimum fixed account rates support the structural integrity of the product’s safety net, which also includes a 25% floor on indexed participation, collectively minimizing investment risk.</data>
  <data key="d4">complements</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
</edge>
<edge source="af34274c-dfee-4fb4-a491-3e2e93de0364" target="c4dbdf51-a4cd-4a65-8903-f269d529eefd">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 reinforces the assurance given in fact_sentence_1 by confirming that all fixed account rates remain above their guaranteed floors, ensuring stability.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="af34274c-dfee-4fb4-a491-3e2e93de0364" target="024598e4-2394-4fad-b636-543f3ffb9225">
  <data key="d3">Guaranteed minimum fixed account rates ensure consistent earnings even in poor markets, supporting the policyholder’s ability to maintain sufficient cash value so that partial withdrawals do not erode the death benefit excessively over time.</data>
  <data key="d4">enhances stability</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
