<edge source="5ba693f1-db68-45ea-a535-eef1cf763796" target="6e42de55-cde0-435f-b499-10c6b12172e2">
  <data key="d3">The disclaimer about past performance not guaranteeing future results supports broader transparency, reinforcing the need to distinguish the product's non-security status by emphasizing caution regarding financial projections.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5ba693f1-db68-45ea-a535-eef1cf763796" target="d95da1e8-f071-414b-b0ad-9b56d2f0e759">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 cautions against relying on historical trends when assessing potential returns; this caution applies particularly given the lack of actual stock ownership described in fact_sentence_1.</data>
  <data key="d4">informs context</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5ba693f1-db68-45ea-a535-eef1cf763796" target="2ec53e58-1461-418f-af0f-33f4dab5f971">
  <data key="d3">Fact sentence 2 warns against assuming future returns based on past data. This reinforces the need for clarity in how indices function, such as the lack of direct fund ownership mentioned in fact sentence 1.</data>
  <data key="d4">reinforces understanding</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5ba693f1-db68-45ea-a535-eef1cf763796" target="6d5cb567-6ee5-41f3-8c36-a83d2ff5c7a3">
  <data key="d3">Since past performance fails to predict future results, relying solely on historical index behavior—even without dividends—is misleading. The absence of dividend inclusion further limits what past figures can indicate.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5ba693f1-db68-45ea-a535-eef1cf763796" target="7e3f4dce-a967-443e-8c1e-f4c1a24f502c">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 cautions that prior index performance is not indicative of future success. This warning becomes particularly relevant given that participation rates may fluctuate annually, meaning even strong past results might not translate into similar future credits.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5ba693f1-db68-45ea-a535-eef1cf763796" target="b080d9ad-b053-459f-8150-83b862b99de1">
  <data key="d3">Fact_sentence_2 cautions against relying on prior performance when predicting future results. This contextualizes the significance of fact_sentence_1’s guarantee, emphasizing that although minimums protect downside, they don’t ensure positive growth beyond those floors.</data>
  <data key="d4">contextualizes</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5ba693f1-db68-45ea-a535-eef1cf763796" target="a416fa11-2b3f-4f38-958d-ff8e13bcbb1a">
  <data key="d3">Acknowledging that past index performance cannot predict future outcomes provides context for understanding why guaranteed minimums exist—to protect against volatility even when history suggests otherwise.</data>
  <data key="d4">informs</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="5ba693f1-db68-45ea-a535-eef1cf763796" target="af34274c-dfee-4fb4-a491-3e2e93de0364">
  <data key="d3">Although past index performance cannot ensure future gains, the presence of guaranteed minimum rates offers a safety net regardless of market fluctuations.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
