  <data key="d3">Describing 'zero' as the hero underscores the absence of downside risk, which complements the practical safeguard offered by the 61-day grace period in preserving policyholder protections.</data>
  <data key="d4">enhances</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="47fe3387-29bc-4869-a3a5-637bc22b6a91" target="15cc61a2-a432-4cb5-8906-a25d63f7e7f6">
  <data key="d3">The concept of “zero” as a protector implies that despite losing surrender value during lapse, the policyholder faces no additional loss beyond what's already accounted for, aligning with the safety net described in the first sentence.</data>
  <data key="d4">enhances</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="47fe3387-29bc-4869-a3a5-637bc22b6a91" target="1fb961d9-6574-4554-b263-906d75b3f515">
  <data key="d3">Describing 'zero' as the hero underscores the safety net of guaranteed minimum returns and no losses from index declines, complementing the contestability clause by reinforcing trust in policy integrity despite potential inaccuracies at inception.</data>
  <data key="d4">enhances</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="47fe3387-29bc-4869-a3a5-637bc22b6a91" target="6e42de55-cde0-435f-b499-10c6b12172e2">
  <data key="d3">The idea that "zero is the hero" reflects the policy’s guarantee against losses from negative index moves, reinforcing why it is distinct from securities products.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="47fe3387-29bc-4869-a3a5-637bc22b6a91" target="d95da1e8-f071-414b-b0ad-9b56d2f0e759">
  <data key="d3">The assertion that zero is the hero reflects the safeguard inherent in index participation without stock ownership, where declines in the underlying index do not lead to financial loss below zero.</data>
  <data key="d4">underpins</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="47fe3387-29bc-4869-a3a5-637bc22b6a91" target="2ec53e58-1461-418f-af0f-33f4dab5f971">
  <data key="d3">Describing zero as the "hero" underscores the guarantee against negative returns, which aligns with the mechanism explained in the first sentence where participants aren't directly exposed to index declines.</data>
  <data key="d4">corroborates</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="47fe3387-29bc-4869-a3a5-637bc22b6a91" target="6d5cb567-6ee5-41f3-8c36-a83d2ff5c7a3">
  <data key="d3">The emphasis on zero being central to risk protection reflects the policy's guarantee against losses from negative index moves, consistent with the structural decision to exclude dividends from performance calculations.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.75</data>
</edge>
<edge source="47fe3387-29bc-4869-a3a5-637bc22b6a91" target="a6b58496-e890-407d-99f3-f8e86cce69dd">
  <data key="d3">The idea that zero represents safety underscores why stable guarantees matter—even when cap rates fluctuate annually.</data>
  <data key="d4">explains</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.65</data>
</edge>
<edge source="47fe3387-29bc-4869-a3a5-637bc22b6a91" target="b080d9ad-b053-459f-8150-83b862b99de1">
  <data key="d3">The assertion that "zero is the hero" reflects the design principle behind the guaranteed minimum rate, where zero serves as a buffer preventing any negative impact from market downturns, thus underpinning the reliability of the cap rate floor.</data>
  <data key="d4">underpins</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="47fe3387-29bc-4869-a3a5-637bc22b6a91" target="a416fa11-2b3f-4f38-958d-ff8e13bcbb1a">
  <data key="d3">The assertion that zero is the hero reflects how the policy protects against financial loss through mechanisms like guaranteed minimums, ensuring participants cannot lose more than zero despite market volatility.</data>
  <data key="d4">justifies</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.95</data>
</edge>
<edge source="47fe3387-29bc-4869-a3a5-637bc22b6a91" target="af34274c-dfee-4fb4-a491-3e2e93de0364">
  <data key="d3">The assertion that zero is the hero reflects the assurance that even in adverse market conditions, losses are prevented—a principle directly enabled by guaranteed minimum rate protections.</data>
  <data key="d4">underpins</data>
  <data key="d2">fact_fact</data>
  <data key="d5">0.85</data>
